          "statement": "The quadratic $p(t)=t^2-t+1/10$ is positive at both sampled endpoints $t=0,1$ but negative at $t=1/2$. Its degree-two Bernstein controls are $1/10,-2/5,1/10$; the negative middle control explains why the all-controls-nonnegative hypothesis in [[thm-bernstein-convex-hull-and-positivity]] does not apply."
