          },
          "generation": {
            "role": "example"
          },
          "statement": "Consider the nonnegative table $(x_i,y_i)=((0,1),(1,0),(2,0),(3,1))$. On the three unit cells, with $t=x-i$ on cell $[i,i+1]$, define\n$$S_0(t)=1-\\frac65t+\\frac15t^3,\\qquad S_1(t)=-\\frac35t(1-t),\\qquad S_2(t)=\\frac35t+\\frac35t^2-\\frac15t^3.$$\nThese pieces form a natural cubic spline interpolating the table, but $S_1(t)<0$ for $0<t<1$. PCHIP on the same data has a flat middle segment at zero and remains between the nonnegative cell endpoints."
