          "statement": "Fix $f(x)=x^2$ on $[-1,1]$. For each integer $n\\ge2$, use the uniform grid $x_j=-1+jh$, $j=0,\\ldots,2n$, with $h=1/n$. The function is smooth and has a strict extremum at zero. On the cell $[-h,0]$, PCHIP's local maximum error is at least $2h^2/27$, so no uniform $Ch^3$ value-error bound on this fixed interval can hold across the extremum."
