    "id": "thm-zero-padded-fft-toeplitz-matvec-is-exact-and-costs-nlogn",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "A zero-padded circulant embedding computes a Toeplitz product in O(N log N)",
    "statement": "Let $m,n\\ge1$, let $T\\in\\mathbb C^{m\\times n}$ be Toeplitz with $T_{ij}=t_{i-j}$ for $0\\le i<m$, $0\\le j<n$, and let $x\\in\\mathbb C^n$. Set $L=m+n-1$ and let $N$ be the least power of two with $N\\ge L$. Define $c\\in\\mathbb C^N$ by\n$$c_\\ell=t_\\ell\\ (0\\le\\ell<m),\\qquad c_{N-d}=t_{-d}\\ (1\\le d<n),$$\nand set every other coordinate to zero. Let $\\widetilde x=(x_0,\\ldots,x_{n-1},0,\\ldots,0)^T\\in\\mathbb C^N$. In exact arithmetic, the first $m$ coordinates of the cyclic convolution $c*_N\\widetilde x$ equal $Tx$.\n\nThe convolution can be computed with three exact length-$N$ DFT calls, pointwise products, and scalar scaling. Its arithmetic count is $O(N\\log_2N)$ for $N\\ge2$ and constant when $N=1$. This is an exact-arithmetic count for the formal exact-constant FFT model; a finite-precision execution is not claimed to be exact.",
