    "id": "lem-complex-hermitian-toeplitz-reflection-recursion",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "Complex Hermitian Toeplitz bordering yields reflection coefficients and positive pivots",
    "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$ and let $T_n=(t_{i-j})_{0\\le i,j<n}$ be Hermitian positive definite, so $t_{-r}=\\overline{t_r}$. For $0\\le k\\le n$, set $T_k=(t_{i-j})_{0\\le i,j<k}$, with $T_0$ empty, and for $0\\le k<n$ set $g_k=(t_1,\\ldots,t_k)^T$, with $g_0$ empty. Define $\\phi_0$ empty and $\\nu_0=t_0$. For each $0\\le k\\le n-2$, let $J_k$ reverse $k$ coordinates, put $c_k=J_k\\overline{g_k}$, and set\n$$\\alpha_{k+1}:=\\frac{t_{k+1}-c_k^*\\phi_k}{\\nu_k},\\qquad \\phi_{k+1}:=\\begin{pmatrix}\\phi_k-J_k\\overline{\\phi_k}\\,\\alpha_{k+1}\\\\ \\alpha_{k+1}\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\nu_{k+1}:=\\nu_k(1-|\\alpha_{k+1}|^2).$$\nEvery denominator used is strictly positive; $T_k\\phi_k=g_k$ and $\\nu_k=t_0-g_k^*\\phi_k>0$ for $0\\le k<n$. Computing through order $n-1$ takes $O(n^2)$ complex arithmetic operations and $O(n)$ working storage. This is the complex matrix-bordering extension; the real ACVF forecast procedure remains [[alg-durbin-levinson-forecast-recursion]].",
