  {
    "id": "def-displacement-rank-generators-and-lower-shift",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Lower-shift displacement rank and generator pairs",
    "statement": "For $A\\in\\mathbb C^{n\\times n}$, $n\\ge1$, let $Z=Z_n$ be the lower shift with $Z_{i+1,i}=1$ for $0\\le i<n-1$ and all other entries zero. Its lower-shift (Stein) displacement is\n$$\\nabla_Z(A):=A-ZAZ^*.$$\nThe **displacement rank** of $A$ with respect to this fixed shift is $\\operatorname{rank}(\\nabla_Z(A))$. A pair of matrices $G,H\\in\\mathbb C^{n\\times r}$ is a **generator of width $r$** when\n$$\\nabla_Z(A)=GH^*.$$\nSuch a factorization is a representation of the displacement, not a factorization of $A$ itself. The term **Toeplitz-like** refers to matrices whose displacement rank is small relative to $n$; the rank bound $r$ must be specified rather than unrestricted. For a family of growing dimensions, a uniform bound means that $r$ is independent of $n$. This definition makes no conditioning, pivot-growth, or numerical-stability assertion.",
    "deps": [
