  {
    "id": "thm-gohberg-semencul-inverse-identity-and-cost",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "The Hermitian positive-definite Gohberg–Semencul formula is exact and quadratic",
    "statement": "Let $T_n=(t_{i-j})_{0\\le i,j<n}$ be Hermitian positive definite, and let $b\\in\\mathbb C^n$. Run [[alg-hermitian-toeplitz-general-rhs-gohberg-semencul-solve]] in exact arithmetic. It returns $x=T_n^{-1}b$. If $u=T_n^{-1}e_0$ and $v=T_n^{-1}e_{n-1}$ are the first and last inverse columns, then\n$$T_n^{-1}=\\frac1{u_0}\\left(L(u)L(u)^*-L(Z_nv)L(Z_nv)^*\\right),\\qquad u_0>0.$$\nThe recursion and four triangular Toeplitz products use $O(n^2)$ complex arithmetic operations and $O(n)$ storage beyond the input, output, and lag vector. This is an exact-arithmetic cost statement and makes no finite-precision stability claim.",
