      "label": "LIN-TT",
      "title": "Tensor train compression and truncation error",
      "companion": "tensor-train-compression-and-truncation-error-examples",
      "requires": [
        "computed-singular-values-and-rank-revealing-factorizations"
      ],
      "description": "{\"scope\": [\"Define finite tensor unfoldings, Tucker/HOSVD, TT cores/bond ranks, canonical gauges and contraction.\", \"Define sequential TT-SVD and rounding with explicit rank or tolerance and zero-rank conventions; prove exact representation absent truncation and Frobenius error <= sqrt(sum discarded unfolding singular-value tails squared).\", \"Prove HOSVD quasioptimal error <= sqrt(d) times best multilinear-rank error, TT contraction/storage and arithmetic costs from actual mode sizes/ranks; CP alternating least squares is a budgeted algorithm with rank-deficient LS branch and monotone objective only for exact block minimization. No best CP rank existence claim.\"], \"proof_route\": \"Use existing SVD/Eckart-Young plus orthogonal tensor projections; telescope pairwise orthogonal discarded terms for TT and apply projection union bound for HOSVD; exhibit rank-jump/illposed CP boundary.\", \"examples\": [\"Rank-one separable grid tensor\", \"Two TT truncations with root-sum-square bound\", \"Large exact TT ranks for a deliberately entangled tensor\"]}",
      "items": [
  {
    "id": "def-finite-tensor-arrays-and-frobenius-inner-product",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Finite tensor arrays and the Frobenius inner product",
    "statement": "Fix a field $\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$, an integer $d\\ge2$, and positive integers $n_1,\\ldots,n_d$. A finite order-$d$ tensor of shape $(n_1,\\ldots,n_d)$ is an array $A=(A_{i_1,\\ldots,i_d})$ indexed by $1\\le i_k\\le n_k$. Its Frobenius inner product and norm are\n$$ \\langle A,B\\rangle_F=\\sum_{i_1=1}^{n_1}\\cdots\\sum_{i_d=1}^{n_d}\\overline{A_{i_1,\\ldots,i_d}}B_{i_1,\\ldots,i_d}, \\qquad \\|A\\|_F=\\sqrt{\\langle A,A\\rangle_F}. $$\nFor a matrix, rank means the dimension of its column image and the Frobenius inner product is the same entrywise formula. The adjoint $M^*$ is conjugate transpose (transpose over $\\mathbb R$).\n\nFor $1\\le k\\le d$, the mode-$k$ unfolding $A_{(k)}$ has $n_k$ rows and $\\prod_{j\\ne k}n_j$ columns. Its row index is $i_k$ and its column index is the remaining tuple in increasing mode order, lexicographically ordered. Its entry at that row and column is the corresponding entry of $A$. For $1\\le k<d$, the cut-$k$ unfolding $A^{\\langle k\\rangle}$ has row tuple $(i_1,\\ldots,i_k)$ and column tuple $(i_{k+1},\\ldots,i_d)$, each lexicographically ordered. These conventions fix all reshapes used below.",
    "deps": [],
    "dependency_level": 0,
    "provenance": {
      "statement": "literature-derived",
      "proof": "not-applicable"
    },
    "sources": {
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "Ivan V. Oseledets, Tensor-Train Decomposition, SIAM Journal on Scientific Computing 33(5) (2011), §§2–4",
          "url": "https://users.math.msu.edu/users/iwenmark/Teaching/CMSE890/TENSOR_oseledets2011.pdf"
        },
        {
          "title": "Tamara G. Kolda and Brett W. Bader, Tensor Decompositions and Applications, SIAM Review 51(3) (2009), §§2–4",
          "url": "https://www.kolda.net/publication/TensorReview.pdf"
        },
        {
          "title": "Lieven De Lathauwer, Bart De Moor, and Joos Vandewalle, A Multilinear Singular Value Decomposition, SIAM Journal on Matrix Analysis and Applications 21(4) (2000), §§2–3",
          "url": "https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~saito/data/tensor/lathauwer-etal_mulilinear-SVD.pdf"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "lem-tensor-unfoldings-are-frobenius-isometries",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "Tensor unfoldings preserve the Frobenius inner product",
    "statement": "For tensors $A,B$ of the same finite shape, every mode unfolding and every cut unfolding preserves the Frobenius inner product and norm.",
    "deps": [
      "def-finite-tensor-arrays-and-frobenius-inner-product"
    ],
    "dependency_level": 1,
    "provenance": {
      "statement": "literature-derived",
