    },
    "sources": {
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "Tamara G. Kolda and Brett W. Bader, Tensor Decompositions and Applications, SIAM Review 51(3) (2009), §2.4",
          "url": "https://www.kolda.net/publication/TensorReview.pdf"
        },
        {
          "title": "Lieven De Lathauwer, Bart De Moor, and Joos Vandewalle, A Multilinear Singular Value Decomposition, SIAM Journal on Matrix Analysis and Applications 21(4) (2000), §2",
          "url": "https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~saito/data/tensor/lathauwer-etal_mulilinear-SVD.pdf"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "def-tucker-multilinear-rank-and-mode-products",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Tucker format, multilinear rank, and mode products",
    "statement": "For a tensor $A\\in\\mathbb F^{n_1\\times\\cdots\\times n_d}$, its multilinear rank is\n$$ \\operatorname{mlrank}(A)=\\bigl(\\operatorname{rank}A_{(1)},\\ldots,\\operatorname{rank}A_{(d)}\\bigr). $$\nIf $U\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times n_k}$, the mode-$k$ product $A\\times_k U$ is the tensor with mode-$k$ size $m$ and entries\n$$ (A\\times_k U)_{i_1,\\ldots,i_{k-1},j,i_{k+1},\\ldots,i_d} =\\sum_{i_k=1}^{n_k}A_{i_1,\\ldots,i_d}U_{j,i_k}. $$\nThe product is bilinear in the entries; no conjugation is used in this tensor contraction.\n\nA Tucker representation with mode ranks bounded by $r=(r_1,\\ldots,r_d)$ is a factorization\n$$ A=G\\times_1 U_1\\times_2\\cdots\\times_d U_d, $$\nwhere $U_k\\in\\mathbb F^{n_k\\times r_k}$ and $G\\in\\mathbb F^{r_1\\times\\cdots\\times r_d}$. Separately, write\n$$ \\mathcal T_r=\\{B\\in\\mathbb F^{n_1\\times\\cdots\\times n_d}:\\operatorname{rank}B_{(k)}\\le r_k\\text{ for each }k\\} $$\nfor the multilinear-rank-bounded set used in approximation statements.",
    "deps": [
      "def-finite-tensor-arrays-and-frobenius-inner-product"
    ],
    "dependency_level": 1,
    "provenance": {
      "statement": "literature-derived",
      "proof": "not-applicable"
    },
    "sources": {
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "Tamara G. Kolda and Brett W. Bader, Tensor Decompositions and Applications, SIAM Review 51(3) (2009), §§2.4, 4",
