  {
    "id": "alg-sequential-tensor-train-svd",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "title": "Sequential tensor-train SVD",
    "statement": "Work in exact arithmetic over $\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$. The input is a tensor $A\\in\\mathbb F^{n_1\\times\\cdots\\times n_d}$ with $d\\ge2$, and exactly one of:\n\n- rank caps $c_1,\\ldots,c_{d-1}\\in\\mathbb N_0$; or\n- absolute tail tolerances $\\tau_1,\\ldots,\\tau_{d-1}\\in[0,\\infty)$.\n\nAt cut $k$, flatten the current remainder with rows $(\\alpha_{k-1},i_k)$ and columns $(i_{k+1},\\ldots,i_d)$, where $\\alpha_0=1$, and compute an exact compact SVD $M_k=U_k\\Sigma_kV_k^*$. Its positive singular values are ordered decreasingly as $\\sigma_1,\\ldots,\\sigma_s$. Under rank caps choose $q_k=\\min(c_k,s)$. Under tolerances choose the least $q_k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,s\\}$ for which $\\sum_{j>q_k}\\sigma_j^2\\le\\tau_k^2$. This set is nonempty because $q_k=s$ gives tail zero. Record the discarded tail\n$$ \\delta_k=\\left(\\sum_{j>q_k}\\sigma_j^2\\right)^{1/2}. $$\n\nReshape the first $q_k$ columns of $U_k$ into core $G_k$ and reshape $\\Sigma_{k,1:q_k}V_{k,1:q_k}^*$ as the next remainder. After cut $d-1$, reshape the remaining matrix as $G_d$. If $q_k=0$, the remainder has zero row dimension; all later ranks and tails are set to zero and the remaining cores are the corresponding empty zero arrays. Thus the zero tensor has all internal ranks zero, a cap zero returns the zero tensor, and a tolerance large enough to select $q_k=0$ does the same. The output is the TT core list and the cut tails $(\\delta_k)$. Any SVD tie at a retained cutoff may be resolved by any orthonormal choice within the tied singular subspace.",
    "deps": [
      "def-finite-tensor-arrays-and-frobenius-inner-product",
      "def-tensor-train-cores-bond-ranks-and-canonical-gauges",
      "thm-singular-value-decomposition"
    ],
    "dependency_level": 2,
    "provenance": {
