  {
    "id": "alg-tensor-train-rounding",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "title": "Tensor-train rounding",
    "statement": "Work in exact arithmetic over $\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$. The input is a valid TT core list for a tensor of order $d\\ge2$ and exactly one of rank caps $c_1,\\ldots,c_{d-1}\\in\\mathbb N_0$ or absolute tail tolerances $\\tau_1,\\ldots,\\tau_{d-1}\\in[0,\\infty)$.\n\n1. **Left orthogonalize without truncation.** For $k=1,\\ldots,d-1$, reshape core $G_k$ into a matrix with rows $(\\alpha_{k-1},i_k)$ and columns $\\alpha_k$. Compute an exact compact SVD $M=U\\Sigma V^*$, replace $G_k$ by the reshape of $U$, and absorb $\\Sigma V^*$ into the next core along their common bond. Omitting zero singular directions is exact. The resulting cores $G_1,\\ldots,G_{d-1}$ are left-isometric.\n\n2. **Truncate from right to left.** For $k=d,d-1,\\ldots,2$, reshape the current $G_k$ into a matrix $M_k$ with rows $\\alpha_{k-1}$ and columns $(i_k,\\alpha_k)$, and compute an exact compact SVD $M_k=U_k\\Sigma_kV_k^*$. If its positive singular values are $\\sigma_1\\ge\\cdots\\ge\\sigma_s>0$, choose $q_{k-1}=\\min(c_{k-1},s)$ for rank caps, or the least $q_{k-1}\\in\\{0,\\ldots,s\\}$ with $\\sum_{j>q_{k-1}}\\sigma_j^2\\le\\tau_{k-1}^2$ for tolerances. Record $\\delta_{k-1}=(\\sum_{j>q_{k-1}}\\sigma_j^2)^{1/2}$. Replace $G_k$ by the reshape of the first $q_{k-1}$ rows of $V_k^*$ and absorb $U_{k,1:q}\\Sigma_{k,1:q}$ into the previous core.\n\nIf $q_{k-1}=0$, the represented tensor becomes zero; set all remaining internal ranks to zero and their unperformed tails to zero. If the input represents zero, return the all-zero-rank representation and zero tails immediately. The output is the rounded core list and all recorded cut tails. No finite-precision error guarantee is part of this exact-arithmetic procedure.",
    "deps": [
      "def-finite-tensor-arrays-and-frobenius-inner-product",
      "def-tensor-train-cores-bond-ranks-and-canonical-gauges",
      "thm-singular-value-decomposition"
