    "statement": "Let $A\\in\\mathbb F^{n_1\\times\\cdots\\times n_d}$, $d\\ge2$, and let $A^{\\langle k\\rangle}$ denote its cut-$k$ unfolding. For sequential TT-SVD, let $r_k$ be its retained bond size and $\\delta_k$ its discarded singular-value tail at cut $k$. For rounding, let the input TT represent $A$ and use the same notation for the output bond sizes and recorded tails. Then both procedures satisfy\n$$ \\|A-\\widehat A\\|_F^2\\le\\sum_{k=1}^{d-1}\\delta_k^2. $$\nIf no positive singular value is discarded, the output is exactly $A$. In full-rank TT-SVD, $r_k=\\operatorname{rank}(A^{\\langle k\\rangle})$ for every cut, and these are the minimal possible TT bond sizes among exact representations.",
