      "description": "{\"scope\": \"genuinely-new periodic lattice-sum algorithm and error separation\\n\\nA: `ewald-periodic-potentials-and-particle-mesh-error`.\\n\\nOn a specified 3D torus, finitely many distinct positions x_i and real charges q_i with sum q_i=0 define the mean-zero periodic Poisson distribution -Delta u=4pi(sum q_i delta_xi). Prove the Fourier distribution solution with zero mode fixed and the Gaussian Ewald decomposition of its off-source values/renormalized self energy. Specify the lattice shape, self subtraction, Gaussian parameter alpha, real/reciprocal cutoffs, output convention and arithmetic model. The naive Coulomb lattice sum is conditional; the periodic mean-zero definition controls the summation convention. Prove absolute convergence of the split sums, alpha independence, explicit Gaussian real-tail/reciprocal-tail bounds using lattice shell counts, and differentiated force bounds away from collisions. Include other boundary conventions only by separate explicit formula/proof.\\n\\nFor particle-mesh Ewald specify charge assignment degree/window, periodic grid, discrete Fourier solver, deconvolution restrictions, force differentiation and self correction. Prove error as real cutoff + reciprocal cutoff + assignment/aliasing + mesh differentiation + arithmetic, with actual window Fourier-decay/smoothness assumptions; O(N log N) FFT work alone is not an accuracy theorem. Point-source potentials are singular: any uniform field error is on a collision-free evaluation set, or is stated for a regularized source norm. N-body time integration, thermodynamic limits and singular mean-field limits remain separate.\\n\\nSame-frontier PC-EWALD suppliers: Gaussian Poisson summation (reuse canonical Poisson theorem if its hypotheses fit), torus distribution Green function and zero mode, lattice shell Gaussian estimates, self limit, assignment Fourier aliases and force derivative bounds. Linear owner FFT; PDE owner periodic Poisson if it supplies the exact torus distribution interface; biology owner PIC consumes only the solver guarantee under matching regularization. B: neutral dipole cell, nonneutral zero-mode obstruction, alpha tradeoff at fixed tolerance, source collision, energy/force consistency. Sources: Ewald 1921 https://doi.org/10.1002/andp.19213690304 ; Darden–York–Pedersen PME https://doi.org/10.1063/1.464397 ; Essmann et al smooth PME https://doi.org/10.1063/1.470117 . Reading pending.\\n\\nResolved preauthoring PME proof design: author two same-A-page suppliers before the force certificate, following the complete PC-EWALD local mesh supplier proof development appendix in research/numerical-analysis-four-category-scaffolds-2026-10-16/linear-audit.md and the resolved supplier section in research/plan-numerical-linear-track.md. Preserve P≥2. The negative-sign unitary FFT recovers charge coefficients with √(M_1M_2M_3)/conj(D_k); exact signed alias indices and derivative factors k+n⊙M are essential. Use the explicit derivative p-series controller for P≥3 and finite piecewise derivative-window enclosures for P=2, with a declared one-sided or symmetric derivative value at knots and no false classical-gradient claim there. Keep real/reciprocal tails, assignment/source aliases, derivative-window aliases, mesh differentiation, self correction and actual arithmetic enclosures separate. Gaussian Poisson summation consumes the published full-rank lattice Poisson theorem with Countable Choice and consistent 2π normalization. No empirical rms estimator supplies a deterministic error bound. This is a planning proof obligation, not completed authoring or review coverage.\", \"proof_route\": [\"On a specified 3D torus, finitely many distinct positions x_i and real charges q_i with sum q_i=0 define the mean-zero periodic Poisson distribution -Delta u=4pi(sum q_i delta_xi). Prove the Fourier distribution solution with zero mode fixed and the Gaussian Ewald decomposition of its off-source values/renormalized self energy. Specify the lattice shape, self subtraction, Gaussian parameter alpha, real/reciprocal cutoffs, output convention and arithmetic model. The naive Coulomb lattice sum is conditional; the periodic mean-zero definition controls the summation convention. Prove absolute convergence of the split sums, alpha independence, explicit Gaussian real-tail/reciprocal-tail bounds using lattice shell counts, and differentiated force bounds away from collisions. Include other boundary conventions only by separate explicit formula/proof.\", \"For particle-mesh Ewald specify charge assignment degree/window, periodic grid, discrete Fourier solver, deconvolution restrictions, force differentiation and self correction. Prove error as real cutoff + reciprocal cutoff + assignment/aliasing + mesh differentiation + arithmetic, with actual window Fourier-decay/smoothness assumptions; O(N log N) FFT work alone is not an accuracy theorem. Point-source potentials are singular: any uniform field error is on a collision-free evaluation set, or is stated for a regularized source norm. N-body time integration, thermodynamic limits and singular mean-field limits remain separate.\", \"Same-frontier PC-EWALD suppliers: Gaussian Poisson summation (reuse canonical Poisson theorem if its hypotheses fit), torus distribution Green function and zero mode, lattice shell Gaussian estimates, self limit, assignment Fourier aliases and force derivative bounds. Linear owner FFT; PDE owner periodic Poisson if it supplies the exact torus distribution interface; biology owner PIC consumes only the solver guarantee under matching regularization. B: neutral dipole cell, nonneutral zero-mode obstruction, alpha tradeoff at fixed tolerance, source collision, energy/force consistency. Sources: Ewald 1921 https://doi.org/10.1002/andp.19213690304 ; Darden–York–Pedersen PME https://doi.org/10.1063/1.464397 ; Essmann et al smooth PME https://doi.org/10.1063/1.470117 . Reading pending.\", \"Resolved preauthoring PME proof design: author two same-A-page suppliers before the force certificate, following the complete PC-EWALD local mesh supplier proof development appendix in research/numerical-analysis-four-category-scaffolds-2026-10-16/linear-audit.md and the resolved supplier section in research/plan-numerical-linear-track.md. Preserve P≥2. The negative-sign unitary FFT recovers charge coefficients with √(M_1M_2M_3)/conj(D_k); exact signed alias indices and derivative factors k+n⊙M are essential. Use the explicit derivative p-series controller for P≥3 and finite piecewise derivative-window enclosures for P=2, with a declared one-sided or symmetric derivative value at knots and no false classical-gradient claim there. Keep real/reciprocal tails, assignment/source aliases, derivative-window aliases, mesh differentiation, self correction and actual arithmetic enclosures separate. Gaussian Poisson summation consumes the published full-rank lattice Poisson theorem with Countable Choice and consistent 2π normalization. No empirical rms estimator supplies a deterministic error bound. This is a planning proof obligation, not completed authoring or review coverage.\"], \"examples\": \"neutral dipole cell, nonneutral zero-mode obstruction, alpha tradeoff at fixed tolerance, source collision, energy/force consistency. The energy/force-consistency example uses the exact declared differentiation and mesh-self correction; distinguish a spectral alternative and state the P=2 knot derivative convention.\"}",
