    "dependency_level": 2,
    "statement": "Input $a<b$, $\\omega\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}$, real $g\\in C^1[a,b]$ with $|g'|\\ge c>0$, complex $f\\in C[a,b]$, an integer $n\\ge2$, and complex-valued $C^1$ functions $\\psi_1,\\ldots,\\psi_n:[a,b]\\to\\mathbb C$ linearly independent over $\\mathbb C$. Also input distinct collocation nodes $a=x_1<\\cdots<x_n=b$. Define $L_\\omega\\psi=\\psi'+i\\omega g'\\psi$, form $A_{jk}=L_\\omega\\psi_k(x_j)$ and $y_j=f(x_j)$. If $A$ is singular, return failure status and no quadrature value. Otherwise solve $Ac=y$ in exact arithmetic, put $p=\\sum_{k=1}^nc_k\\psi_k$, and return\n$$Q_L=p(b)e^{i\\omega g(b)}-p(a)e^{i\\omega g(a)}$$\nwith $A,c$, and $\\kappa_2(A)=\\|A\\|_2\\|A^{-1}\\|_2$, where vector norms are Euclidean and $\\|A\\|_2=\\sup_{\\|v\\|_2=1}\\|Av\\|_2$ is the induced matrix norm. This is a finite collocation procedure; residual and conditioning claims for the nonsingular branch are stated separately on this page. Rounded factorization error is outside this exact-arithmetic definition.",
    "strategy": "Input $a<b$, $\\omega\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}$, real $g\\in C^1[a,b]$ with $|g'|\\ge c>0$, complex $f\\in C[a,b]$, an integer $n\\ge2$, and complex-valued $C^1$ functions $\\psi_1,\\ldots,\\psi_n:[a,b]\\to\\mathbb C$ linearly independent over $\\mathbb C$. Also input distinct collocation nodes $a=x_1<\\cdots<x_n=b$. Define $L_\\omega\\psi=\\psi'+i\\omega g'\\psi$, form $A_{jk}=L_\\omega\\psi_k(x_j)$ and $y_j=f(x_j)$. If $A$ is singular, return failure status and no quadrature value. Otherwise solve $Ac=y$ in exact arithmetic, put $p=\\sum_{k=1}^nc_k\\psi_k$, and return\n$$Q_L=p(b)e^{i\\omega g(b)}-p(a)e^{i\\omega g(a)}$$\nwith $A,c$, and $\\kappa_2(A)=\\|A\\|_2\\|A^{-1}\\|_2$, where vector norms are Euclidean and $\\|A\\|_2=\\sup_{\\|v\\|_2=1}\\|Av\\|_2$ is the induced matrix norm. This is a finite collocation procedure; residual and conditioning claims for the nonsingular branch are stated separately on this page. Rounded factorization error is outside this exact-arithmetic definition.",
