    "statement": "Input $a<b$, $\\omega\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}$, a real phase $g\\in C^{r+1}[a,b]$ with $|g'|\\ge c>0$, a complex amplitude $p\\in C^r[a,b]$, an integer $r\\ge1$, and a certified real bound $M\\ge\\|T_g^rp\\|_\\infty$. Compute\n$$S_r(p)=\\sum_{j=0}^{r-1}\\frac{(-1)^j}{(i\\omega)^{j+1}}\\left[\\frac{T_g^jp(x)}{g'(x)}e^{i\\omega g(x)}\\right]_a^b,\\qquad \\epsilon_r=\\frac{(b-a)M}{|\\omega|^r}.$$\nReturn $(S_r(p),\\epsilon_r)$. The nonstationary recurrence and the need for the certified derivative bound are specified in [[thm-na-nonstationary-oscillatory-integration-by-parts]]. If exact phase moments are available, they may instead be passed as exact moment data to a Filon rule; this algorithm makes no general closed-form claim for nonlinear phases.",
