    "statement": "Let $a<b$, $\\omega\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}$, $f\\in C^2[a,b]$ be complex-valued, and $g\\in C^3[a,b]$ be real-valued with $|g'|\\ge c>0$. Use the endpoint Lagrange rule from [[alg-na-filon-nodal-moment-quadrature]] and put $r=f-p_n$. If $\\mu_j=\\int_a^b\\ell_j e^{i\\omega g}$ and the rule uses $\\widehat\\mu_j$ with $|\\widehat\\mu_j-\\mu_j|\\le\\epsilon_j$, then\n$$|I_\\omega(f,g;[a,b])-Q_n|\\le\\frac{|T_gr(a)/g'(a)|+|T_gr(b)/g'(b)|+(b-a)\\|T_g^2r\\|_\\infty}{|\\omega|^2}+\\eta_n.$$\nWith exact moments $\\eta_n=0$, this is an $O(|\\omega|^{-2})$ endpoint-interpolation error bound. The constant depends on the fixed amplitude, phase, nodes, and derivative norms.",
