        {
          "id": "def-barycentric-rational-quotient",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Barycentric rational quotient with support values and reduced poles",
          "deps": [
            "lem-barycentric-denominator-polynomial-nonzero"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "statement": "Let $k\\ge1$, let $z_1,\\ldots,z_k\\in\\mathbb C$ be distinct support nodes, let\n$f_1,\\ldots,f_k\\in\\mathbb C$ be data, and let each weight $w_j\\in\\mathbb C$ be\nnonzero. Define the cleared polynomials\n$$P(z)=\\sum_{j=1}^{k}w_jf_j\\prod_{\\ell\\ne j}(z-z_\\ell), \\qquad Q(z)=\\sum_{j=1}^{k}w_j\\prod_{\\ell\\ne j}(z-z_\\ell).$$\nThe **barycentric rational quotient** is the rational function $r=P/Q$.\nAway from the support nodes this equals\n$$r(z)= \\frac{\\sum_{j=1}^{k} w_jf_j/(z-z_j)} {\\sum_{j=1}^{k} w_j/(z-z_j)}.$$\nAt a support node its value is given by the cleared quotient $P(z_j)/Q(z_j)$.\nA **pole** means a zero of the denominator after all common polynomial\nfactors of numerator and denominator have been canceled.",
          "provenance": {
