          ],
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Pedro Gonnet, Stefan Güttel, and Lloyd N. Trefethen, Robust Padé Approximation via SVD, Section 2",
                "url": "https://people.maths.ox.ac.uk/trefethen/gonnet_guettel_trefethen.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $m,n\\ge0$, $R>0$, and\n$f(z)=\\sum_{k=0}^\\infty c_kz^k$ for $|z|<R$, with the series convergent\nthere. Suppose $q_0=1,q_1,\\ldots,q_n$ solve the full normalized\nPadé moment equations of [[alg-pade-coefficient-matching]]. Define\n$p_k=\\sum_{j=0}^{\\min(k,n)}q_jc_{k-j}$ for $0\\le k\\le m$, and\n$p(z)=\\sum_{k=0}^mp_kz^k$, $q(z)=\\sum_{j=0}^nq_jz^j$. Then\n$$\nf(z)-\\frac{p(z)}{q(z)}=O(z^{m+n+1})\\quad\\text{as }z\\to0.\n$$\nThis is a local Taylor-matching statement only; it gives no pole-location\nclaim and no guarantee about analytic continuation beyond the neighborhood\nwhere $f$ is given.\n\nHere $h(z)=O(z^M)$ as $z\\to0$ means there are constants $C,\\delta>0$ such\nthat $|h(z)|\\le C|z|^M$ whenever $0<|z|<\\delta$."
