  {
    "id": "def-three-dimensional-delaunay-and-weighted-regular-lower-hull",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Three-dimensional Delaunay and weighted regular triangulations by lifting",
    "deps": [
      "def-indexed-geometric-site-set",
      "lem-lifted-power-sphere-determinant-identity",
      "def-lexicographic-lift-tie-break"
    ],
    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 2,
    "statement": "For a weighted site $(p,w)$, define its power distance from $x\\in\\mathbb R^3$ by\n$$\\pi_{(p,w)}(x)=\\|x-p\\|^2-w.$$\nIts lifted point is $\\widehat p=(p,\\|p\\|^2-w)\\in\\mathbb R^4$. A lower face of the lifted convex hull is a face supported by a nonvertical hyperplane $z=\\ell(x)$ with every lifted site on or above that hyperplane. The projection of the union of lower faces is the **regular subdivision** of the projected sites; a simplex in that subdivision has an empty power sphere, meaning its common power distance is no larger than that of any input site.\n\nThe lex-refined lift is interpreted over the ordered rational-function field of [[def-lexicographic-lift-tie-break]], using one fixed finite universe of all input sites. When every weight is zero, the regular subdivision is the ordinary 3D Delaunay subdivision and power spheres are circumspheres. A weighted site is **original-hidden** if its unperturbed lift is not a vertex of any lower face of the original lifted convex hull, and **formal-hidden** if its lex-refined lift is not a vertex of any lower face of the fixed formal lifted convex hull. These notions can differ; the algorithm's `hidden` report means formal-hidden. A nonsimplicial lower face is refined with the same fixed-universe lexicographic lift convention. For projected affine dimension below three, the algorithm reports `lower-dimensional` with that dimension and the exact deduplicated site list, and makes no tetrahedralization claim. A tetrahedral output is claimed only on the full-dimensional branch with nondegenerate projected bases.",
    "source_path": "items/def-three-dimensional-delaunay-and-weighted-regular-lower-hull.md",
    "provenance": {
