    "dependency_level": 3,
    "statement": "Let $ABCD$ be a strictly convex planar quadrilateral in counterclockwise boundary order. Lift its four sites using the common formal heights of [[def-lexicographic-lift-tie-break]]. Let $g_{AC}$ and $g_{BD}$ be the piecewise-affine interpolants on the two diagonal triangulations. Define each interpolant's integral over the quadrilateral as the sum over its two triangles of triangle area times the average of the three vertex heights. If the lifted point $D$ lies strictly below the affine plane through the lifts of $A,B,C$ (the illegal-incircle sign by the coefficientwise determinant identity), then\n$$\\int_{ABCD}g_{BD}<\\int_{ABCD}g_{AC}$$\nin the lexicographic order of the formal lift field.",
