  {
    "id": "alg-hlr-core-svd-recompression-with-tolerance",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "title": "Core-SVD recompression with rank and error tolerances",
    "statement": "**Input:** A field $\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$, positive integers $m,n$, a finite factor list $U_s\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times r_s}$ and $V_s\\in\\mathbb F^{n\\times r_s}$ representing $M=\\sum_s U_sV_s^*$, a rank cap $0\\le k\\le\\min(m,n)$, and a Frobenius tolerance $\\delta\\ge0$. The conjugate transpose $M^*$ and Frobenius norm are those of [[def-finite-tensor-arrays-and-frobenius-inner-product]].\n\n**Procedure:** Concatenate the factors as $U=[U_1\\ \\cdots\\ U_p]$ and $V=[V_1\\ \\cdots\\ V_p]$, so $M=UV^*$. Take compact singular value decompositions $U=Q_UR_U$ and $V=Q_VR_V$, where the columns of $Q_U,Q_V$ are orthonormal and span the respective column spaces. Form the core $C=R_UR_V^*$ and compute an SVD $C=P\\Sigma Q^*$. Let its positive singular values be $s_1\\ge\\cdots\\ge s_t>0$. Find the smallest $q\\in\\{0,\\ldots,\\min(k,t)\\}$ for which $e_q:=(\\sum_{j>q}s_j^2)^{1/2}\\le\\delta$. If no such $q$ exists, return **tolerance-not-met**. Otherwise return **success** with factors $\\widehat U=Q_UP_{[:,1:q]}\\Sigma_q$ and $\\widehat V=Q_VQ_{[:,1:q]}$, where $\\Sigma_q=\\operatorname{diag}(s_1,\\ldots,s_q)$, and the exact discarded-tail certificate $e_q$; when $q=0$, use empty $m\\times0$ and $n\\times0$ factors.\n\nThe compact decompositions retain only positive singular directions. If the factor list is empty or its represented matrix is zero, then $t=0$ and the procedure returns the rank-zero representation because $\\delta\\ge0$. Any SVD choices in repeated singular subspaces are permitted. No result is returned when the requested cap cannot certify the tolerance.",
    "deps": [
      "def-finite-tensor-arrays-and-frobenius-inner-product",
      "thm-singular-value-decomposition"
    ],
