  {
    "id": "alg-hlr-compress-exact-lu-factors",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "title": "Compress exact block LU factors with local tolerances",
    "statement": "**Input:** An exact factorization $A=LU$ of a square matrix $A\\in\\mathbb F^{n\\times n}$, where $\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$ and $n\\ge1$, with $L$ block lower triangular and $U$ block upper triangular on a common ordered cluster partition; an integer rank cap $k\\ge1$; and a nonnegative local Frobenius tolerance for each admissible off-diagonal block of $L$ and $U$. The factorization $A=LU$ is supplied as a hypothesis, not computed by this procedure.\n\n**Procedure:** Copy every dense nearfield block and every diagonal block exactly. For each strictly lower admissible block $D_b\\in\\mathbb F^{m_b\\times n_b}$ of $L$ and each strictly upper admissible block $D_b$ of $U$, form the one-pair factor list $(D_b,I_{n_b})$, representing $D_b=D_bI_{n_b}^*$, and pass it to [[alg-hlr-core-svd-recompression-with-tolerance]] with effective cap $\\min(k,m_b,n_b)$ and its given local tolerance. Keep structural zero blocks zero. If any compression reports **tolerance-not-met**, return that status and the factor/block identity. Otherwise return $\\widehat L,\\widehat U$ and the local discarded-tail bounds $\\epsilon_b^L,\\epsilon_c^U$ reported by the recompressions. The exact diagonal blocks preserve block triangularity; no claim is made that the compressed factors are exact factors of $A$.",
    "deps": [
