    "kind": "algorithm",
    "title": "Tolerance-controlled H-matrix block addition",
    "statement": "**Input:** Two H-matrix representations $A,B$ on the same block-cluster partition $\\mathcal P$, a rank cap $k\\ge1$, and for each far block $b\\in\\mathcal P$ a factor-sum tree with node tolerances whose total is at most $\\delta_b\\ge0$. The tree leaves are the exact factors of $A_b$ and $B_b$.\n\n**Procedure:** For each near block, store the exact dense sum $A_b+B_b$ and report local error $e_b=0$. For each far block, run [[alg-hlr-bottom-up-recompression]] on its factor-sum tree with cap $k$. If any block returns **tolerance-not-met**, return that status and the block identity; otherwise store the root factors, report the certified error bound $e_b$ returned by that routine, and retain the block partition. The input's node budgets sum to at most $\\delta_b$, so $e_b\\le\\delta_b$ by the bottom-up error guarantee.",
