    "id": "alg-hlr-block-product",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "title": "Tolerance-controlled H-matrix block product",
    "statement": "**Input:** H-matrix representations $A\\in\\mathbb F^{I\\times K}$ and $B\\in\\mathbb F^{K\\times J}$, a recursively generated output block-cluster partition as in [[def-hlr-cluster-trees-and-geometric-admissibility]], a rank cap $k\\ge1$, local tolerances $\\delta_b\\ge0$ for far output blocks, and for each output block $b=(\\tau,\\sigma)$ a finite intermediate-cluster family $\\mathcal K_b$ partitioning $K$ such that the restrictions $A_{\\tau\\kappa}$ and $B_{\\kappa\\sigma}$ are available in dense or factorized form for each $\\kappa\\in\\mathcal K_b$. For a far output block, its factor-sum tree has one exact product term for each $\\kappa\\in\\mathcal K_b$ and node tolerances totaling at most $\\delta_b$. This compatibility condition is part of the input.\n\n**Procedure:** For each output block, use the exact identity $C_b=\\sum_{\\kappa\\in\\mathcal K_b}A_{\\tau\\kappa}B_{\\kappa\\sigma}$. If the output block is near, form and store this dense sum exactly and report $e_b=0$. For a far output block, convert each product term to factor form: $UV^*\\cdot PQ^*=U(V^*P)Q^*$ when both factors are low rank; $UV^*\\cdot D=U(D^*V)^*$ and $D\\cdot PQ^*=(DP)Q^*$ when one factor is dense; and $D_1D_2=D_1(D_2^*)^*$ when both are dense. These formulas produce factors with matching inner dimensions. Run [[alg-hlr-bottom-up-recompression]] on the resulting finite factor-sum tree with cap $k$. If any block returns **tolerance-not-met**, return that status and block identity; otherwise store the root factors and its certified bound $e_b\\le\\delta_b$.",
