    "id": "thm-hlr-approximate-factorization-residual-and-inverse-error",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Compressed block LU factors have a residual and inverse certificate",
    "statement": "Let $A\\in\\mathbb F^{n\\times n}$ be invertible over $\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$, $n\\ge1$, and let $A=LU$ be an exact block lower-upper factorization. Suppose [[alg-hlr-compress-exact-lu-factors]] returns $\\widehat L,\\widehat U$ and exact local discarded-tail errors $e_b^L,e_c^U$. All operations and norms in this theorem are exact. Put $\\epsilon_L=(\\sum_b(e_b^L)^2)^{1/2}$, $\\epsilon_U=(\\sum_c(e_c^U)^2)^{1/2}$, $\\widehat A=\\widehat L\\widehat U$, and $\\eta=\\epsilon_L\\|U\\|_F+\\|\\widehat L\\|_F\\epsilon_U$. Then\n\n$$\\|A-\\widehat A\\|_F\\le\\eta\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\\|A-\\widehat A\\|_2\\le\\eta.$$\n\nIf $q=\\|A^{-1}\\|_2\\eta<1$, then $\\widehat A$ is invertible and\n\n$$\\|\\widehat A^{-1}-A^{-1}\\|_2\\le\\frac{\\|A^{-1}\\|_2^2\\eta}{1-q}.$$",
