      ],
      "description": "{\"scope\": [\"Define an (epsilon,delta) oblivious l2 subspace embedding S with 0<epsilon<1 for fixed finite-dimensional subspace; distinguish fixed-subspace probability from a single S preserving all subspaces.\", \"Define sketch-and-solve LS xhat minimizing ||S(Ax-b)||, computed through canonical QR/SVD with rank/failure status. If S preserves all vectors in span(A,b) within squared norms (1±epsilon), prove ||Axhat-b||² <= ((1+epsilon)/(1-epsilon)) min_x||Ax-b||². A guarantee only on Ran(A) is insufficient for this unqualified residual theorem.\", \"Define iid Gaussian embedding with declared m and prove m>=C epsilon^-2(d+log(1/delta)) suffices by chi-square tail, finite net and operator norm transfer, all locally proved.\", \"Define leverage-score row sampling with probabilities p_i>=beta ell_i/d, rescale selected rows, specify zero leverage rows and replacement; prove embedding with m>=C d log(d/delta)/(beta epsilon²) by locally proved matrix concentration. Sparse CountSketch/SRHT are separate optional algorithm variants and require their actual dimension/coherence theorem, owned here if promised.\", \"Define sketch-based right preconditioner and prove conditioned spectrum after embedded QR and exact span/rank premises; retain physical residual and computed solve errors separately.\"], \"proof_route\": \"Embedding inequalities sandwich original/sketched objective; Gaussian quadratic mgf plus net; derive matrix Chernoff/Bernstein needed by leverage sampling instead of citing as external proof. QR preconditioner singular values follow norm embedding.\", \"examples\": [\"Overdetermined regression sketch\", \"Embedding Ran(A) but missing residual direction\", \"Leverage-zero rows and highly coherent design\"]}",
      "items": [
  {
    "id": "alg-sketch-and-solve-least-squares",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "title": "Rank-aware sketch-and-solve least squares",
    "statement": "Input $A\\in\\mathbb K^{n\\times p}$, $b\\in\\mathbb K^n$, a supplied sketch\n$S\\in\\mathbb K^{m\\times n}$, and a finite nonnegative integer SVD sweep\nbudget $N$, where $\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$. Form\n$C=SA$ and $c=Sb$, and call\n[[alg-rank-thresholded-least-squares-by-svd]] on $(C,c)$ with threshold\n$\\tau=0$ and budget $N$.\n\nIf the call returns exact-arithmetic convergence with an exact SVD record,\nreturn `success`, the exact rank $r=\\operatorname{rank}(C)$, the canonical\nminimum-norm vector $\\widehat x=C^+c$, and the separately computed sketched\nand physical residuals $\\|C\\widehat x-c\\|_2$ and\n$\\|A\\widehat x-b\\|_2$. The exact-arithmetic solve-error certificate is\nzero. If the SVD call returns `inconclusive`, return its status and supplied\npartial diagnostics without claiming a minimizer. In finite precision, return\nthe computed candidate and the two residual reports separately; mark the rank\n`unverified` unless a certified interval separates every singular-value\ncomparison from zero, and report a solve-error certificate only when the\nsolver supplies one. No finite-precision accuracy guarantee is part of this\nprocedure.",
