  {
    "id": "lem-moore-penrose-products-are-orthogonal-projectors",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "The Moore-Penrose products are orthogonal projectors",
    "statement": "Let $M\\in\\mathbb F^{p\\times q}$ be any finite real or complex matrix, and let $M^\\dagger$ be its unique Moore-Penrose inverse. Then $P=MM^\\dagger$ and $Q=M^\\dagger M$ are self-adjoint idempotents. The range of $P$ is $\\operatorname{Ran}(M)$, and the range of $Q$ is $\\operatorname{Ran}(M^\\dagger)$. Thus both are orthogonal projections. If $M$ has full row rank, then $MM^\\dagger=I_p$.",
