  {
    "id": "def-psd-nystrom-approximation",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "The positive-semidefinite Nyström approximation",
    "statement": "Let $\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$, let $A\\in\\mathbb F^{n\\times n}$ be Hermitian positive semidefinite with $n\\ge1$, and let $S\\in\\mathbb F^{n\\times s}$ with $s\\ge0$ be any finite sketch matrix. Put $W=S^*AS\\in\\mathbb F^{s\\times s}$. The **Nyström approximation** associated with $(A,S)$ is\n$\\widehat A_{\\mathrm{nys}}=AS\\,W^\\dagger S^*A$.\n\nThe Moore-Penrose inverse is defined for every finite matrix, including singular $W$, and is unique by the dependencies. No rank, sampling, or probabilistic condition is part of this definition.",
