    "id": "thm-planar-fmm-operation-count-under-linear-list-assumptions",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Planar FMM operation count under explicit linear-size tree and list bounds",
    "statement": "Let $N\\ge1$ and $p\\ge1$. Suppose the finite quadtree and recursive interaction decomposition supplied to [[alg-planar-laplace-fmm-fixed-order]] are linear-size level-restricted and have bounded lists in the exact sense of [[def-finite-planar-quadtree-fmm-pair-lists]]: $T,V\\le C\\,N$, $K:=|\\mathcal F|\\le C\\,T$, and $J:=|\\mathcal N|\\le C\\,N$ for a constant $C$ independent of $N,p$. Counting each complex addition, multiplication, division by a nonzero number, coefficient copy, cell-pair inspection, and evaluation of a fixed logarithm branch at one argument as one operation, the FMM passes and direct near evaluation use at most\n$$C_0\\bigl(N(p+1)+(T+K)(p+1)^2+V+J\\bigr)$$\noperations for an absolute implementation constant $C_0$. Hence the total counted work is $O(N(p+1)^2)$, and therefore $O(Np^2)$ for $p\\ge1$. The input quadtree construction and point-to-cell preprocessing are not included; a highly clustered input must report its actual tree depth, node count, and list/traversal counts before a linear-in-$N$ conclusion is made.",
