    "id": "thm-planar-fmm-global-potential-force-error",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Global planar FMM potential and derivative error",
    "statement": "Assume the collision-free exact-arithmetic branch of [[alg-planar-laplace-fmm-fixed-order]] with order $p\\ge1$. For each target $i$ in leaf $D_i$, let $\\mathcal F_i=\\{(C,D)\\in\\mathcal F:i\\in I_D\\}$ be its far cell interactions. For $(C,D)\\in\\mathcal F_i$ put $R_{CD}=|c_D-c_C|$, $\\rho_{CD}=(a_C+a_D)/R_{CD}<1$, and $Q_C=\\sum_{j\\in I_C}|q_j|$. If $u_i$ is the exact fixed-branch logarithmic potential and $\\widetilde u_i$ the algorithm output, then\n$$|u_i-\\widetilde u_i|\\le\\sum_{(C,D)\\in\\mathcal F_i}\\frac{Q_C\\rho_{CD}^{p+1}}{(p+1)(1-\\rho_{CD})}.$$\nIf $g_i=\\sum_{j\\ne i}q_j/(z_i-z_j)$ and $\\widetilde g_i$ is the algorithm's complex derivative output, then\n$$|g_i-\\widetilde g_i|\\le\\sum_{(C,D)\\in\\mathcal F_i}\\frac{Q_C}{R_{CD}}\\frac{\\rho_{CD}^{p}}{1-\\rho_{CD}}.$$\nNear interactions are exact. The second estimate is branch-independent; no floating-point rounding error is included.",
