          "title": "Level-uniform 1D Poisson smoothing and approximation bounds",
          "statement": "Let $N=2M\\ge4$, $h=1/N$, and let $A_h\\in\\mathbb R^{(N-1)\\times(N-1)}$ have diagonal $2/h$, adjacent off-diagonal entries $-1/h$, and all other entries zero. This is the Dirichlet stiffness matrix for the uniform one-dimensional Poisson mesh. Let $P\\in\\mathbb R^{(N-1)\\times(M-1)}$ linearly interpolate from the coarse nodes at even fine indices: set coarse endpoint values $v_0=v_M=0$, $(Pv)_{2j}=v_j$, and $(Pv)_{2j+1}=(v_j+v_{j+1})/2$ wherever these are interior fine indices. Put $A_H=P^{\\mathsf T}A_hP$, $C=I-PA_H^{-1}P^{\\mathsf T}A_h$, and $S=I-A_h/\\lambda_{\\max}(A_h)$. Then for every integer $\\nu\\ge1$ and every fine vector $e$,\n\n$$\\|CS^\\nu e\\|_{A_h}^2\\le\\frac{2}{2\\nu+1}\\|e\\|_{A_h}^2.$$\n\nThe separate estimates proved below are the exact approximation bound\n$\\|Cw\\|_{A_h}^2\\le(h/2)\\|A_hw\\|_2^2$ and smoothing bound\n$\\|A_hS^\\nu e\\|_2^2\\le4\\,[h(2\\nu+1)]^{-1}\\|e\\|_{A_h}^2$; their constants are compatible and independent of $N$.",
