          "statement": "Assume a two-dimensional hierarchy with levels $j=0,\\ldots,L$ of sizes\n$N_j=4^j$, so the finest level has $N=N_L=4^L$ unknowns and each coarsening\nstep reduces the size by four. Suppose each level has constant $c>0$ work per\nunknown, the base solve has bounded positive cost, and the cycle is as in\n[[alg-finite-galerkin-v-cycle]]. The V-cycle has one coarse call; the W-cycle\nhas two. Both have $\\Theta(N)$ arithmetic work under these hypotheses, with\ndifferent geometric sums.",
