          "title": "Rank-revealing QR sweeps give exact mixed canonical gauge",
          "statement": "Let a nonzero finite open-boundary TT have order $d\\ge2$, and choose a center window $[s,t]$ with $1\\le s\\le t\\le d$ and $t-s+1\\in\\{1,2\\}$. There is an exact rank-revealing QR transformation of its cores that preserves the represented array, makes every core $k<s$ left-isometric and every core $k>t$ right-isometric, and removes exactly the dependent coordinates on each swept bond. No independent column direction is truncated; only exactly dependent directions are removed.\n\nFor each reshaped matrix $M$, the rank-revealing QR used here scans its columns in their fixed order, retaining a column exactly when it increases the span. It applies Gram–Schmidt to the retained columns, writes all other columns in that orthonormal span, and records the resulting permutation and coefficient factor.",
