          "statement": "Let a finite open-boundary TT have order $d\\ge2$ and be in the following mixed gauge about a one-site or two-site center window $J=[k,k+w-1]$, where $w\\in\\{1,2\\}$: every core strictly left of $J$ is left-isometric and every core strictly right of $J$ is right-isometric. The center coefficient array has shape $r_{k-1}\\times n_k\\times\\cdots\\times n_{k+w-1}\\times r_{k+w-1}$, with boundary ranks interpreted as one, and $x$ is its vectorization in the fixed lexicographic order. Hold every core outside $J$ fixed. Contracting the fixed prefix and suffix defines a linear embedding $E$ from center coefficients to the full tensor space. Then $E^*E=I$, so $\\|Ex\\|_F=\\|x\\|_2$. For every finite Hermitian Hamiltonian input $H$, the effective matrix\n$$H_{\\mathrm{eff}}:=E^*HE$$\nis Hermitian and satisfies\n$$\\langle Ex,HEx\\rangle_F=x^*H_{\\mathrm{eff}}x.$$",
