        {
          "id": "prop-na-exact-local-dmrg-update-does-not-increase-energy",
          "kind": "proposition",
          "title": "An exact local DMRG ground solve does not increase Rayleigh energy",
          "statement": "Let $\\psi_0=Ex_0$ be a normalized finite MPS in mixed canonical gauge about a one-site or two-site center, with $\\|x_0\\|_2=1$. Let $H_{\\mathrm{eff}}=E^*HE$ be its effective Hermitian matrix, and replace the center by the deterministic unit ground vector $x_* $ of $H_{\\mathrm{eff}}$, giving $\\psi_*=Ex_*$. Then $\\psi_*$ is normalized and\n$$\\mathcal E_H(\\psi_*)\\le\\mathcal E_H(\\psi_0).$$\nThis claim is before any bond truncation.",
