        {
          "id": "thm-na-dmrg-sweep-truncation-energy-increase-bound",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "TT discarded weights bound the post-sweep DMRG energy increase",
          "statement": "Let $\\psi_0$ be a normalized finite MPS/TT state with a supplied concrete open-boundary TT core list or periodic trace presentation contracting to $\\psi_0$, and let $H$ be a finite Hermitian Hamiltonian on the same coefficient space. Run [[alg-na-alternating-tensor-optimization-and-effective-eigenproblems]] for one full forward/backward sweep of a fixed width $w\\in\\{1,2\\}$, with $M=1$ and no rank caps, from that presentation using exact local solves and exact SVD splits; call its normalized unrounded output $\\psi_*$. Apply exact TT rounding with rank caps $c_1,\\ldots,c_{d-1}\\in\\mathbb N_0$, obtaining $\\widetilde\\psi$ and discarded tails $\\delta_1,\\ldots,\\delta_{d-1}$. Put $\\tau=(\\sum_{k=1}^{d-1}\\delta_k^2)^{1/2}$. If $\\tau<1$, define $\\phi=\\widetilde\\psi/\\|\\widetilde\\psi\\|_F$. Then\n$$\\mathcal E_H(\\phi)\\le \\mathcal E_H(\\psi_0)+4\\|H\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\\tau.$$\nIn particular,\n$$\\mathcal E_H(\\phi)-\\mathcal E_H(\\psi_*)\\le4\\|H\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\\tau.$$\nNo normalized-output claim is made when $\\tau\\ge1$.",
