        {
          "id": "thm-na-convergent-exact-dmrg-sweeps-are-coordinatewise-stationary",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "Convergent fixed-rank exact sweeps are coordinatewise stationary",
          "statement": "Fix a finite Hermitian Hamiltonian $H$ on the coefficient space of the states. Consider an infinite sequence obtained by repeatedly applying one full no-truncation sweep of [[alg-na-alternating-tensor-optimization-and-effective-eigenproblems]], starting from a supplied concrete open-boundary TT core list or periodic trace presentation representing a normalized state, with fixed bond dimensions and a fixed finite list of one-site or two-site update windows. Assume the canonical core arrays at every stage of each sweep are bounded and converge componentwise in one consistent gauge to a single normalized canonical core tuple. Then the limit is **coordinatewise stationary**, meaning that for each update window, its limiting center vector minimizes the Rayleigh quotient of the effective Hermitian Hamiltonian over all unit center vectors with the other limiting cores fixed. In particular, each limiting center is a lowest eigenvector of its limiting effective Hamiltonian. This is conditional on the stated convergence; it asserts neither convergence of DMRG nor global minimality.",
