          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "statement": "Consider the scalar damped oscillator with mass $M=1$, damping coefficient $C=1/2$, and stiffness $K=2$. Its quadratic polynomial is $P(\\lambda)=\\lambda^2+(1/2)\\lambda+2$. The first companion pencil is\n$$L(\\lambda)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\lambda+1/2&2\\\\-1&\\lambda\\end{bmatrix}.$$\nThis example checks its finite roots and the companion eigenvector lift.",
