            "thm-first-companion-pencil-is-strong-linearization"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "statement": "Take the grade-two matrix polynomial $P(\\lambda)=\\operatorname{diag}(1,\\lambda^2)$, so $n=m=2$, $\\det P(\\lambda)=\\lambda^2$, and $A_2=\\operatorname{diag}(0,1)$ is singular. The finite root $\\lambda=0$ and the infinite root are different projective eigenvalues. Their algebraic and geometric multiplicities are computed directly below.",
          "source_path": "items/ex-infinite-polynomial-eigenvalue-from-singular-leading-coefficient.md",
