      ],
      "description": "{\"scope\": [\"Fix finite real/complex A (n by n), B (n by m), Q=C* C positive semidefinite and R positive definite. Define continuous stabilizability by existence of K with A-BK Hurwitz and continuous detectability by existence of L with A-LC Hurwitz; discrete versions replace Hurwitz by Schur stability. Prove equivalent PBH rank tests with Re(lambda)>=0 or |lambda|>=1, including eigenvalues on the boundary. Stabilizability/detectability are exact hypotheses or certified rank/stability inputs; they are not inferred from an observed small residual.\", \"CARE is A*X+XA-XGX+Q=0 with G=B R^-1 B*. Under continuous stabilizability/detectability prove existence and uniqueness of positive semidefinite stabilizing X, A-GX Hurwitz, and that H=[[A,-G],[-Q,-A*]] has no imaginary-axis eigenvalues and its n-dimensional stable invariant space is a graph Ran([I;X]). Include infinite-horizon quadratic-cost characterization only as the necessary local existence/uniqueness proof, with square-integrable controls, finite cost and transversality/terminal decay justified. CTRL1 may consume this; LIN-RIC does not consume CTRL1.\", \"DARE is X=Q+A*XA-A*XB(R+B*XB)^-1B*XA. Under discrete stabilizability/detectability prove unique positive semidefinite stabilizing X with R+B*XB positive definite and Ac=A-B(R+B*XB)^-1 B*XA Schur. Define N=[[A,0],[-Q,I]], M=[[I,G],[0,A*]], prove regularity and stable deflating graph N[I;X]=M[I;X] Ac, n stable eigenvalues and no unit-circle eigenvalues. Singular A is allowed; infinite generalized eigenvalues are handled homogeneously. Do not use inverse(A).\", \"Define finite-budget ordered Schur CARE and ordered-QZ DARE numerical procedures, stable/unstable selection with explicit certified half-plane/unit-circle separation, graph block U1 inversion, X=U2 U1^-1, Hermitian symmetrization, factor/conditioning/range and inconclusive statuses. Prove exact graph-to-ARE identity. Computed Schur/QZ backward errors are generally unstructured: report actual Riccati residual and symmetry defect, and do not claim nearby positive Q/R or preserved Hamiltonian structure from an arbitrary nearby pencil.\", \"For CARE candidate Xhat Hermitian let Ac=A-GXhat be certified Hurwitz and L(E)=Ac*E+E Ac. With kappa>=||L^-1||_(F->F), r>=||F(Xhat)||_F, g>=||G||2, find rho>0 with kappa(r+g rho²)<=rho and 2 kappa g rho<1. Prove unique Hermitian exact root in the closed Frobenius rho-ball by E=-L^-1 F(Xhat)+L^-1(EGE). To certify the stabilizing branch, additionally provide W positive definite with Ac*W+W Ac negative definite and 2||W||2 g rho smaller than its negative-definiteness margin. Norm/spectral inequalities are outward-certified by VAL owners; a residual alone is insufficient.\", \"For DARE candidate Xhat Hermitian require R+B*Xhat B positive definite, Ac(Xhat) Schur, and Stein derivative D(E)=Ac* E Ac-E invertible. Derive an explicit Lipschitz bound L_D for the derivative on a radius rho-ball using a verified positive lower bound for R+B*X B there. With kappa>=||D^-1||, require kappa(r+L_D rho²/2)<=rho and kappa L_D rho<1. Prove unique root in that ball and a separate Schur-stability certificate from W-Ac*W Ac positive definite plus the explicit Ac perturbation bound. Do not transplant CARE residual constants to DARE.\", \"Define finite-budget continuous Newton-Kleinman policy iteration from supplied stabilizing K0: solve (A-BKj)* Xj+Xj(A-BKj)=-(Q+Kj*R Kj), then Kj+1=R^-1B*Xj. Under the stated continuous standard hypotheses and exact solves prove every new closed loop stabilizing, Xj positive semidefinite and nonincreasing, convergence to stabilizing X, and local quadratic rate using a uniformly bounded local Lyapunov inverse. For inexact solves require a separate residual/descent/stability safeguard with line search and certified margins; arbitrary approximate solves inherit none of these guarantees.\", \"Define discrete structure-preserving doubling A0=A,G0=G,H0=Q; Aj+1=Aj(I+GjHj)^-1Aj, Gj+1=Gj+Aj(I+GjHj)^-1Gj Aj*, Hj+1=Hj+Aj*Hj(I+GjHj)^-1Aj. Prove inverses exist from PSD Gj,Hj; prove symmetry/PSD via equivalent factored identities and the doubled graph/pencil relation. Under standard stabilizability/detectability/no-unit-circle hypotheses prove Hj tends to stabilizing DARE solution and a quantified eventual quadratic rate with constants depending on closed-loop spectral separation. Critical/unit-circle cases and finite-precision structure loss are excluded or explicit failure/inconclusive outcomes, not covered by this theorem.\", \"Local condition number is inverse Lyapunov/Stein derivative; prove sensitivity and graph-subspace perturbation bounds retaining spectral sep and ||U1^-1||. Dense operation counts use actual Schur/QZ/Lyapunov arithmetic; numerical acceptance requires returned Riccati residual, positive R+B*XB where applicable, symmetry defect and closed-loop stability certificate.\"], \"proof_route\": \"Build PBH/stabilizability/detectability and semigroup/Stein decay first. Prove finite-horizon value matrices monotone/bounded via a supplied stabilizing feedback, pass to infinite horizon with exact finite-energy/transversality estimates, and derive ARE; detectability rules out nonstable unobserved directions and gives stable graph plus uniqueness. Prove Hamiltonian/symplectic graph identities algebraically, then reuse LIN-SCHUR/QZ and Sylvester machinery for computation. Kleinman uses Lyapunov energy identity with nonnegative gain-difference term; doubling uses exact rational squaring of stable/unstable graph maps plus separated spectrum. Residual certificates use contraction on the explicit matrix ball and independent Lyapunov stability margins. All are local complete proof obligations, not source-only suppliers.\", \"examples\": [\"Scalar CARE with two roots and only one stabilizing branch\", \"DARE with singular A and infinite generalized pencil eigenvalue\", \"Nearly imaginary-axis/unit-circle closed-loop mode inflates sep inverse and makes tiny residual inconclusive\", \"Unstabilizable unstable mode or undetectable unstable mode violates promised existence\", \"Scalar exact Newton-Kleinman steps versus an inexact Lyapunov solve losing stability\", \"SDA PSD blocks and reported finite precision symmetry defect\"]}",
