      "description": "{\"scope\": [\"Reuse alg-kalman-filter, def-linear-gaussian-state-space-model-with-independent-noises, lem-one-step-kalman-gaussian-conditioning (which already proves Joseph identity) and thm-kalman-filter-is-exact-posterior. Do not restate Gaussian filtering, Joseph algebra or posterior exactness as new items. New algorithm is an explicitly numerical factor implementation of that canonical covariance/mean map, with finite horizon and arithmetic/factorization statuses.\", \"Inputs are rectangular factors L0,LQk,LRk of PSD P0,Qk,Rk, exact finite Fk,Hk and data, with canonical innovation Sk positive definite. Factors may have zero columns/rank. Prediction QR on [Fk Lplus, LQk]* returns lower factor Lminus whose product is Fk Pplus Fk*+Qk. For fixed square storage zero-pad rectangular factors; zero state/noise pivots are permitted, innovation block must be full rank.\", \"For measurement update form Z=[[LR,H Lminus],[0,Lminus]], padded with zero columns as necessary, and compute QR of Z* so its adjoint factor is lower block triangular [[L11,0],[L21,L22]]. Prove L11 L11*=S, L21 L11*=Pminus H*, L22 L22*=canonical posterior covariance. Mean update is mplus=mminus+L21 z with L11 z=innovation; gain if needed is L21 L11^-1 through triangular solves. Only innovation factor requires positive diagonal; singular L22 is admissible. No subtractive covariance downdate is needed.\", \"Prove with stable Householder QR under NA-02 completed local reflector/range premises: computed lower factor is exact triangular factor of (Z+DeltaZ)(Z+DeltaZ)* with ||DeltaZ||_F<=eta ||Z||_F for an explicit eta=C(dim)u/(1-C(dim)u), plus separately accounted product/input-factor errors. Hence nearby joint covariance error <=(2eta+eta²)||Z||_F². The represented posterior covariance L22 L22* is PSD exactly as a product. This nearby joint covariance may introduce correlations or perturb model blocks: do not claim backward stability within the original independent-noise state-space model without a separate structured perturbation proof.\", \"Prove innovation triangular-solve residual/forward bounds with sigma_min(L11)>0, and perturbation bounds for the block Schur complement/conditional mean retaining ||S^-1||, ||Pminus H*|| and data scale. Positive innovation lower bound must dominate joint perturbation to identify nearby covariance update. Finite-horizon propagation sums per-step factor/product/solve errors with explicitly derived Lipschitz factors; no uniform-in-time stability or accuracy follows without detectability/stability/conditioning assumptions proved here if advertised.\", \"Compare the canonical subtractive update and existing Joseph identity only as algebraic context: numerical cancellation can make a directly rounded Pminus-KSK* indefinite, whereas L22 product is PSD. Do not promise a stored rounded covariance matrix formed from L22 is PSD in exact represented entries unless formed/rounded with an additional certified symmetric factor interpretation. Posterior statistics remain inherited with the original AC assumptions; numerical matrix identities alone require no new choice.\"], \"proof_route\": \"Use canonical one-step block covariance and Gaussian/Joseph supplier. Gram-matrix block multiplication plus QR gives exact numerical equivalence, including semidefinite rank loss. Use NA-02 exact orthogonal representative/backward QR error to obtain a nearby prearray, then algebraic Gram perturbation and Schur-complement resolvent identity. Triangular residual bounds and explicitly conditioned finite-horizon recursion supply actual error guarantees, with input uncertainty and arithmetic error separated.\", \"examples\": [\"Canonical ex-kalman-filter-singular-prior-positive-innovation rerun through rectangular square roots without new statistical example claim\", \"Nearly noiseless observation amplifies innovation solve error\", \"Two-scale covariance where subtractive floating update loses PSD\", \"Nonzero factor residual and PSD represented L22 product with perturbed joint covariance\"]}",
