    "statement": "Let $\\Omega=\\mathbb C\\setminus(-\\infty,0]$. For every $z\\in\\Omega$, an\nadmissible integer $m\\ge0$ with $\\operatorname{Re}(z+m)>0$ exists by the\nArchimedean property [[lem-archimedean-property-from-completeness]]. Choose\nany such $m$ and set\n\n$$\\ell(z)=\\ell_+(z+m)-\\sum_{j=0}^{m-1}\\operatorname{Log}(z+j),$$\n\nwhere the sum is empty if $m=0$ and $\\ell_+$ and $\\operatorname{Log}$ are\ndefined in [[def-loggamma-right-halfplane-branch]]. The next lemma proves that\nthis value is independent of the admissible $m$ and satisfies\n$e^{\\ell(z)}=\\Gamma(z)$.\nThis is a continued branch of log-Gamma, not a separate principal\n$\\operatorname{Log}(\\Gamma(z))$."
