      ]
    },
    "forward_refs": [],
    "statement": "The coefficient recurrence in [[def-airy-initial-value-series]] makes both\nseries solve $y''=zy$. In a residue class $k\\equiv r\\pmod 3$, successive\nnonzero terms have absolute ratio\n\n$$\\frac{|z|^3}{(k+3)(k+2)}.$$\n\nIf the ratio of each term after a chosen first omitted term is bounded by\n$q<1$, that class's tail is at most the first omitted term's absolute value\ndivided by $1-q$. The series and their first two derivative series converge\nlocally uniformly on $\\mathbb C$."
  },
  {
    "id": "lem-erf-series-geometric-tail",
    "deps": [
      "def-fresnel-erf-and-hypergeometric-series",
      "def-complex-exponential",
      "lem-complex-exponential-series-converges-everywhere",
      "thm-termwise-differentiation-of-complex-power-series",
