      "def-complex-line-integral-over-a-rectifiable-path",
      "thm-riemann-stieltjes-and-parametric-contour-integrals-agree"
    ],
    "dependency_level": 1,
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "Error-function series geometric tail bound",
    "justified_by": [],
    "provenance": {
      "statement": "ai-altered",
      "proof": "ai-altered"
    },
    "sources": {
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "DLMF, §7.6(i), equation 7.6.1",
          "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/7.6"
        },
        {
          "title": "N. M. Temme, “Numerical aspects of special functions,” Acta Numerica 17 (2008), §2",
          "url": "https://ir.cwi.nl/pub/11612/11612C.pdf"
        }
      ]
    },
    "forward_refs": [],
    "statement": "For the $k$th term $e_k$ of the $\\operatorname{erf}$ series in\n[[def-fresnel-erf-and-hypergeometric-series]],\n\n$$\\frac{|e_{k+1}|}{|e_k|} =\\frac{|z|^2}{k+1}\\frac{2k+1}{2k+3} \\le\\frac{|z|^2}{k+1}.$$\n\nThe displayed quotient is asserted when $e_k\\ne0$. At $z=0$, every $e_k=0$, so the series and every tail are zero; the corresponding division-free inequality $|e_{k+1}|\\le |z|^2|e_k|/(k+1)$ holds there as well.\n\nThus, if $|z|^2/(K+2)=q<1$, the tail after terms $0,\\ldots,K$ is bounded by\n$|e_{K+1}|/(1-q)$. The series converges locally uniformly. For every\npiecewise-$C^1$ path $\\gamma:[0,1]\\to\\mathbb C$ with $\\gamma(0)=0$ and\n$\\gamma(1)=z$, it equals\n$$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt\\pi}\\int_\\gamma e^{-t^2}\\,dt,$$\nwhere the complex line integral is defined by\n[[def-complex-line-integral-over-a-rectifiable-path]]. In particular, the\nstraight-segment integral has this value, and the integral is path-independent."
  },
  {
    "id": "lem-fresnel-series-geometric-tail",
    "deps": [
      "def-fresnel-erf-and-hypergeometric-series",
