      "description": "{\"scope\": \"genuinely-new finite Gaussian integral algorithms\\n\\nA: `gaussian-basis-integral-recurrences-and-boys-error`.\\n\\nInput finitely many Cartesian Gaussian primitives (polynomial times exp(-a|x-A|²), a>0), real centers and contraction coefficients. Define overlap, kinetic, attraction and two-electron Coulomb integrals as mathematical integrals. Prove absolute convergence including Coulomb singularities; Gaussian product theorem by completing squares; polynomial derivative/raising recurrences by differentiation under an explicit integrable dominating function. Reduce Coulomb integrals using 1/r=(2/sqrt(pi)) integral_0^infinity exp(-t²r²)dt with justified Tonelli and a change of variables to Boys F_m(T)=integral_0^1 t^(2m) exp(-Tt²)dt, m>=0,T>=0. Define finite primitive/contracted integral procedure with a declared recurrence ordering, memoization/work model and error budget. Establish Boys Taylor remainder for small T, positive quadrature enclosure on bounded T, and scaled incomplete-gamma/large-T tail bounds. Prove upward/downward recurrence error amplification and domain-based direction switch. Screening skips a block only with a proved bound (e.g. Coulomb Cauchy–Schwarz), and reports total discarded integral/energy bound rather than claiming exact sparsity.\\n\\nNew suppliers owned PC-GINT: Gaussian moment integrals with parameter derivatives; integral representation and recurrence identities; Boys stable-branch error; positive Coulomb bilinear form/Cauchy–Schwarz; tensor contraction error propagation into PC-VAR energy/gradient, with n/r norms explicit. Reuse canonical quadrature and NA01 arithmetic; no HF postulate used. B: same-center s-orbitals exact formula; small-T cancellation in upward recurrence; highly contracted coefficients; overlap near dependence; screening bound accumulated over all discarded blocks. Sources: Obara–Saika recurrence https://doi.org/10.1063/1.450106 ; McMurchie–Davidson https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-9991(78)90092-X ; Helgaker–Jørgensen–Olsen Molecular Electronic-Structure Theory https://doi.org/10.1002/9781119019572 . Reading pending.\", \"proof_route\": [\"Input finitely many Cartesian Gaussian primitives (polynomial times exp(-a|x-A|²), a>0), real centers and contraction coefficients. Define overlap, kinetic, attraction and two-electron Coulomb integrals as mathematical integrals. Prove absolute convergence including Coulomb singularities; Gaussian product theorem by completing squares; polynomial derivative/raising recurrences by differentiation under an explicit integrable dominating function. Reduce Coulomb integrals using 1/r=(2/sqrt(pi)) integral_0^infinity exp(-t²r²)dt with justified Tonelli and a change of variables to Boys F_m(T)=integral_0^1 t^(2m) exp(-Tt²)dt, m>=0,T>=0. Define finite primitive/contracted integral procedure with a declared recurrence ordering, memoization/work model and error budget. Establish Boys Taylor remainder for small T, positive quadrature enclosure on bounded T, and scaled incomplete-gamma/large-T tail bounds. Prove upward/downward recurrence error amplification and domain-based direction switch. Screening skips a block only with a proved bound (e.g. Coulomb Cauchy–Schwarz), and reports total discarded integral/energy bound rather than claiming exact sparsity.\", \"New suppliers owned PC-GINT: Gaussian moment integrals with parameter derivatives; integral representation and recurrence identities; Boys stable-branch error; positive Coulomb bilinear form/Cauchy–Schwarz; tensor contraction error propagation into PC-VAR energy/gradient, with n/r norms explicit. Reuse canonical quadrature and NA01 arithmetic; no HF postulate used. B: same-center s-orbitals exact formula; small-T cancellation in upward recurrence; highly contracted coefficients; overlap near dependence; screening bound accumulated over all discarded blocks. Sources: Obara–Saika recurrence https://doi.org/10.1063/1.450106 ; McMurchie–Davidson https://doi.org/10.10