    "statement": "Write $\\mathbb N_0=\\{0,1,2,\\ldots\\}$. For $m\\in\\mathbb N_0$ and $T\\in\\mathbb R$, define the finite-integral extension\n$$F_m(T)=\\int_0^1 t^{2m}\\exp(-Tt^2)\\,dt.$$\nThe **Boys function** is the restriction to the conventional domain $T\\ge0$. The extension to negative $T$ is used only for ordinary center derivatives at the boundary value $T=0$; the finite evaluator below accepts no negative argument.\nFor $s>0$ and $T>0$, write the lower incomplete-gamma integral as\n$$\\gamma(s,T)=\\int_0^T u^{s-1}\\exp(-u)\\,du.$$\nThe complete Euler Gamma function $\\Gamma(s)$ has the existing meaning in [[def-euler-gamma-function]], namely $\\Gamma(s)=\\int_0^\\infty u^{s-1}e^{-u}\\,du$ for real $s>0$.\n\nThe integrand defining $F_m$ is continuous on $[0,1]$ and positive on $(0,1]$, so $F_m(T)$ exists, is positive, and, for $T\\ge0$, satisfies $F_m(T)\\le1/(2m+1)$. The index $m$ is an arbitrary nonnegative integer; no fixed maximum order is part of this definition."
  },
  {
    "id": "def-finite-gaussian-basis-variational-energy-and-gradient",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Finite tensor contractions and their variational energy and gradient",
    "deps": [],
    "dependency_level": 0,
    "provenance": {
