    },
    "statement": "Let $a,b>0$, $A,B\\in\\mathbb R^3$, $p=a+b$, $\\mu=ab/p$, and $P=(aA+bB)/p$. Then for every $x\\in\\mathbb R^3$,\n$$\\exp(-a\\|x-A\\|_2^2)\\exp(-b\\|x-B\\|_2^2)=\\exp(-\\mu\\|A-B\\|_2^2)\\exp(-p\\|x-P\\|_2^2).$$\nFor any multi-indices $\\alpha,\\beta\\in\\mathbb N_0^3$, the polynomial factor $(x-A)^\\alpha(x-B)^\\beta$ is a finite polynomial in $x-P$ of total degree at most $|\\alpha|+|\\beta|$. Moreover, $P=(a/p)A+(b/p)B$ lies on the closed segment from $A$ to $B$."
