      "description": "{\"scope\": \"New conservative finite-volume flux/update, consistency and compact weak-limit theorem with actual convergence/hypotheses; continuous weak PDE definitions imported.\", \"proof_route\": \"Multiply each cell update by cell averages of a smooth compactly supported test function, sum over cells and time levels, telescope shared interface fluxes, and pass to the limit using strong L¹_loc convergence and continuity of f/F. Boundary/tail terms require their own control. Compactness is a premise here, not a consequence of conservation alone.\", \"examples\": \"conservative Godunov flux passing a shock speed; a bounded sequence without convergence; a weak limit that violates entropy admissibility.\"}",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-locally-bounded-distributional-weak-solution",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Locally bounded distributional weak solutions of scalar laws",
          "statement": "Let $T>0$, let $f\\colon\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuous, and let\n$u_0\\in L^\\infty(\\mathbb R)\\cap L^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\mathbb R)$. A measurable\nfunction $u\\colon\\mathbb R\\times(0,T)\\to\\mathbb R$ is a **locally bounded\ndistributional weak solution** of $u_t+f(u)_x=0$ with initial datum $u_0$ if\nfor every bounded interval $I\\subset\\mathbb R$ and every $T'<T$ it is\nessentially bounded on $I\\times(0,T')$, and, for every\n$\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R\\times(-\\infty,T))$,\n$$ \\int_0^T\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\bigl(u\\varphi_t+f(u)\\varphi_x\\bigr)\\,dx\\,dt +\\int_{\\mathbb R}u_0(x)\\varphi(x,0)\\,dx=0. $$\nThe integrals are local: if a test is supported in $I\\times[-S,T']$ with $I$\nbounded and $T'<T$, the local essential bound makes $u$ bounded on\n$I\\times(0,T']$, and continuity of $f$ makes $f(u)$ bounded on that bounded\nrange. The initial integral is finite because $u_0$ is locally integrable and\n$\\varphi(\\cdot,0)$ is compactly supported. This is the local\nintegrability version of the weak identity in\n[[def-distributional-weak-solution-of-a-scalar-conservation-law]], whose\npublished formulation assumes a global $L^\\infty$ bound. This definition adds\nno entropy inequality or strong local $L^1$ trace requirement.",
          "deps": [
            "def-scalar-conservation-law-and-flux",
            "def-distributional-weak-solution-of-a-scalar-conservation-law"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "strategy": "Define the local essential-bound condition and weak identity for tests that may meet t=0.",
          "axiom_base": "No choice principle is used.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "H. De Sterck and P. Ullrich, Introduction to Computational PDEs, Chapter 3, complete chapter, PDF pp. 81–106",
