      "description": "{\"scope\": \"New monotone finite-volume L1/BV/entropy stability and convergence incl Helly+temporal compactness/initial trace; continuous entropy uniqueness imported literally.\", \"proof_route\": \"Prove order preservation/range bounds and TVD; establish temporal translation estimates; supply the missing local Helly/BV compactness lemma by a rational-point diagonal argument (uniform local variation and bounds give L¹_loc subsequences). Pass the conservative update and discrete entropy inequality to the limit; use the published Kruzhkov uniqueness/contraction theorem to identify all subsequential limits. Carry the source theorem’s mesh-to-time ratio premise and the chosen piecewise-linear time interpolant. The published entropy-existence theorem requires u₀∈L¹∩L∞ and DC+CC; use it on that global-data branch only. For nonintegrable globally bounded BV data, supply the local-limit existence/initial-trace proof in this pair before using the published local contraction theorem to identify the limit.\", \"examples\": \"Godunov and Lax–Friedrichs monotone flux under CFL; shock captured with correct Rankine–Hugoniot speed; a conservative but nonmonotone weak limit that is not entropy admissible.\"}",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-bounded-bv-data-on-line",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Bounded BV data on the real line",
          "statement": "Let $u$ be an almost-everywhere equivalence class of measurable functions on\n$\\mathbb R$ with $u\\in L^\\infty(\\mathbb R)\\cap L^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\mathbb R)$,\nusing the quotient convention of\n[[def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions]], the essentially bounded\nclass of [[def-l-infinity-on-a-measure-space]], and the local integrability\nconvention of [[def-locally-integrable-function-on-r-n]]. For $h>0$ define\n$$D_hu(x):=u(x+h)-u(x),\\qquad \\operatorname{TV}_{\\mathrm{tr}}(u):=\\sup_{h>0}\\frac1h\\int_{\\mathbb R}|D_hu(x)|\\,dx,$$\nwhere the integral may be $+\\infty$. The **bounded BV class on the line**\n$\\mathrm{BV}_b(\\mathbb R)$ consists of those classes for which\n$\\operatorname{TV}_{\\mathrm{tr}}(u)<\\infty$; we write\n$\\operatorname{TV}(u):=\\operatorname{TV}_{\\mathrm{tr}}(u)$.\n\nThis translation-variation convention is the standard one-dimensional BV\nseminorm on bounded locally integrable classes. It is unchanged by modifying\n$u$ on a null set, because each translate of a null set is null. It does not\nrequire $u\\in L^1(\\mathbb R)$: every bounded constant function belongs to\n$\\mathrm{BV}_b(\\mathbb R)$ and has variation $0$.",
          "deps": [
