        {
          "id": "lem-monotone-fv-update-preserves-range-and-tvd",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Invariant range, TVD and time increments for a monotone finite-volume update",
          "statement": "Let $u_0\\in\\mathrm{BV}_b(\\mathbb R)$ and put $V:=\\operatorname{TV}(u_0)$.\nLet $U^n=(U_j^n)_{j\\in\\mathbb Z}$ be generated by\n[[def-monotone-finite-volume-entropy-scheme]] under its full invariant-interval\nCFL bound. Define the update map\n$$H(a,b,c):=b-\\lambda\\bigl(F(b,c)-F(a,b)\\bigr).$$\nThen $H$ is nondecreasing in each coordinate on $I^3$ and $H(s,s,s)=s$ for\n$s\\in I$. Consequently,\n$$a_-\\le U_j^n\\le a_+\\quad(j\\in\\mathbb Z,\\ n\\ge0),\\qquad \\sum_{j\\in\\mathbb Z}|U_{j+1}^n-U_j^n|\\le V\\quad(n\\ge0).$$\nMoreover, for every $n\\ge0$,\n$$\\frac h\\tau\\sum_{j\\in\\mathbb Z}|U_j^{n+1}-U_j^n|\\le (L_1+L_2)V.$$\nFor a sequence $x=(x_j)_{j\\in\\mathbb Z}$, the notation\n$\\|x\\|_1:=\\sum_{j\\in\\mathbb Z}|x_j|$ is used only when this sum is finite;\n$x\\vee y$ and $x\\wedge y$ mean the coordinatewise maximum and minimum.",
          "deps": [
