    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Fortin operator for a discrete constraint",
    "statement": "Let $V,Q,b$ be as in [[def-na-stokes-zero-mean-pressure-and-velocity-spaces]], and let $V_h\\subset V$, $Q_h\\subset Q$ be finite-dimensional subspaces. A **Fortin operator** is a bounded linear map $\\Pi_h:V\\to V_h$ for which there is a constant $C_F$ such that\n$$\\|\\Pi_hv\\|_V\\le C_F\\|v\\|_V\\quad(v\\in V),\\qquad b(\\Pi_hv,q_h)=b(v,q_h)\\quad(v\\in V,\\ q_h\\in Q_h).$$\nThe second condition is exact constraint preservation. It does not assert $\\operatorname{div}\\Pi_hv=\\operatorname{div}v$ pointwise.",
