      "description": "{\"scope\": \"Define MUSCL finite-volume reconstruction, a concrete minmod limiter, ENO stencil selection, WENO5-JS weights and a documented improved critical-point variant; distinguish finite-volume cell-average reconstruction from nodal finite differences. Prove second-order smooth-region reconstruction where the limiter is inactive; prove scalar TVD for a stated flux/limiter/CFL update by Harten's incremental form. Prove WENO polynomial reproduction/consistency and optimal smooth-region order under explicit smoothness and weight asymptotics; near critical points state the actual JS order, not automatic fifth order. Include the scalar linear monotonicity/order barrier. Systems characteristic reconstruction is defined but receives no automatic scalar TVD theorem.\", \"proof_route\": \"Solve reconstruction moment equations; Taylor-expand candidate polynomials and smoothness indicators with uniform remainders; derive nonlinear weight asymptotics including epsilon scaling. Derive nonnegative incremental coefficients and sum their variation estimate. Give a concrete critical-point counterexample when hypotheses fail.\", \"examples\": \"smooth advection, extrema clipping, Burgers shock, WENO critical point, oscillatory unlimited reconstruction.\"}",
