          "statement": "Work in nondimensional coordinates with $u(x)=x^2+x^3$ and reconstruct the face $x=0$, the interface between cells $I_{-1}$ and $I_0$. This is a first-order critical point: $u'(0)=0$ and $u''(0)=2$. If the WENO-JS parameter is scaled as $\\epsilon_h=h^4$, the cell-average face state has error $\\frac{54}{95}h^4+O(h^5)$, so this branch is fourth order at the face. With the fixed $\\epsilon_0>0$ of [[thm-na-weno-js-fixed-epsilon-fifth-order-reconstruction]], the theorem's fifth-order branch applies; with the same $\\epsilon_h$, the WENO-Z comparison has error $O(h^6)$ on this polynomial.",
