      "requires": [
        "high-resolution-tvd-eno-and-weno-methods"
      ],
      "description": "{\"scope\": \"Define convex invariant sets and convex entropy pairs for systems. Prove a first-order local Lax–Friedrichs/HLL invariant-domain update under a stated invariant Riemann-average hypothesis and CFL convex-combination coefficients; prove ideal-gas density/internal-energy positivity on the explicitly admitted wave-speed branch. Define entropy variables, two-point entropy-conservative flux and dissipative entropy-stable flux. Prove the semidiscrete cell entropy inequality from the exact Tadmor jump condition and positive semidefinite dissipation. Fully discrete entropy needs its own time-step theorem. Define a convex scaling positivity limiter and prove cell-average conservation plus positive quadrature-node states; do not claim cellwise pointwise positivity from finitely many nodes without a separate argument.\", \"proof_route\": \"Convexity of admissible Euler set; decompose updates into invariant Riemann averages. Multiply flux balances by entropy variables, telescope entropy potentials and bound dissipation. Limiter takes the maximal admissible scaling toward a positive mean; prove preservation and smooth-data accuracy only with a strict positive margin.\", \"examples\": \"near-vacuum Euler, entropy residual, conservative positivity rescaling, entropy-stable but insufficiently resolved shock.\"}",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-pe03-convex-invariant-domain",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Convex invariant domains for a one-step update",
          "deps": [],
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "statement": "Let $m,N\\ge1$, let $\\mathcal A\\subseteq\\mathbb R^m$ be a state domain, and let\n$\\Phi:\\mathcal A^N\\to\\mathcal A^N$ be a one-step update on $N$ cell states.\nA set $K\\subseteq\\mathcal A$ is **convex** if\n$\\theta U+(1-\\theta)V\\in K$ for every $U,V\\in K$ and $\\theta\\in[0,1]$.\nIt is a **convex invariant domain for $\\Phi$** if it is convex and\n$\\Phi(K^N)\\subseteq K^N$. The word invariant refers only to this stated\none-step map and its stated admissible inputs; it asserts no invariance for a\ndifferent flux, time integrator, or exact Riemann evolution.",
          "strategy": "Give the typed definition and exact scope; no preservation property is inferred for another map.",
          "justified_by": [],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J.-L. Guermond and B. Popov, Invariant Domains and First-Order Continuous Finite Element Approximation for Hyperbolic Systems",
                "url": "https://people.tamu.edu/~guermond/PUBLICATIONS/guermond_popov_sinum_hyperbolic_systems_2016.pdf",
                "locator": "§2.2, Definitions 2.3–2.4, PDF pp. 3–4; complete 24-page article read"
              }
            ]
          }
