        {
          "id": "def-pe03-first-order-hll-finite-volume-update",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "First-order finite-volume update using supplied HLL speeds",
          "deps": [
            "def-hyperbolic-system-and-characteristic-families",
            "def-hll-two-wave-flux"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "statement": "Let $F:\\mathcal A\\to\\mathbb R^m$ be the flux of the one-dimensional system in\n[[def-hyperbolic-system-and-characteristic-families]]. On a periodic uniform\nmesh of $N\\ge2$ cells of width $h>0$, let $U_i\\in\\mathcal A$ be the cell means\nand put $\\nu=\\Delta t/h\\ge0$. At each face $(i+1/2)$ choose explicit speeds\n$S_{L,i+1/2}<0<S_{R,i+1/2}$ and evaluate the middle branch of the HLL flux\n[[def-hll-two-wave-flux]] on $(U_i,U_{i+1})$. The **first-order HLL update** is\n$$U_i^+=U_i-\\nu\\bigl(\\widehat F_{i+1/2}-\\widehat F_{i-1/2}\\bigr),\\qquad i\\pmod N.$$\nThe speeds are supplied data. Neither this definition nor later algebraic\nresults assert that they enclose the wave speeds of an exact nonlinear Riemann\nsolution.",
