    ],
    "dependency_level": 2,
    "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$. If $d=1$, let $\\mathcal T_h$ be a finite oriented interval mesh of $\\Omega=(a,b)$, $a<b$, from [[def-pe04-one-dimensional-interval-mesh-and-broken-polynomials]]; if $d\\ge2$, let $\\mathcal T_h$ be a finite matching affine simplicial mesh of $\\Omega$. Let $\\beta\\in\\mathbb R^d$ be constant, and let $u_h$ solve [[def-pe04-upwind-dg-transport-discretization]] with inflow data $g$. Assume Countable Choice when $d\\ge2$, as required by the affine-simplex Green supplier; no choice assumption is needed for the interval branch. Write $\\Gamma_+=\\{x\\in\\partial\\Omega:\\beta\\cdot n>0\\}$ and $\\Gamma_- =\\{x\\in\\partial\\Omega:\\beta\\cdot n<0\\}$. For an interior facet $F=K^-\\cap K^+$ choose a unit normal $n_F$ from $K^-$ to $K^+$ and write $[u_h]=u_h^+-u_h^-$. In dimension one, integrals over facets and boundary points mean sums with respect to zero-dimensional surface measure. Then\n$$\\frac12\\frac{d}{dt}\\sum_{K\\in\\mathcal T_h}\\|u_h\\|_{L^2(K)}^2+\\frac12\\sum_{F\\text{ interior}}\\int_F|\\beta\\cdot n_F|[u_h]^2\\,dS+\\frac12\\int_{\\Gamma_+}(\\beta\\cdot n)u_h^2\\,dS+\\frac12\\int_{\\Gamma_-}|\\beta\\cdot n|(u_h-g)^2\\,dS=\\frac12\\int_{\\Gamma_-}|\\beta\\cdot n|g^2\\,dS.$$\nThe equality is understood in $\\mathbb R\\cup\\{+\\infty\\}$. It is a finite energy balance whenever $\\int_{\\Gamma_-}|\\beta\\cdot n|g^2\\,dS<\\infty$ at the time in question; otherwise both sides are $+\\infty$ and give no finite inflow bound. In particular, zero inflow data give a nonincreasing semidiscrete $L^2$ norm. This result is semidiscrete and makes no claim about a time integrator.",
