          "statement": "Let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^3$ have a finite matching affine tetrahedral mesh $\\mathcal T$ as in [[def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes]]. The H(curl) and H(div) graph-space conventions used below carry their stated Countable Choice assumptions. Choose one orientation for every mesh edge and face and the ambient orientation for each tetrahedron, with incidence signs given by [[def-oriented-simplicial-cell-chains]]. Write $t_e$ for the unit tangent in the chosen direction of an edge $e$, and $n_F$ for the unit normal determined by the chosen orientation of a face $F$ and the ambient orientation. On a tetrahedron $K$ with barycentric coordinates $\\lambda_0,\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2,\\lambda_3$, list the vertices in any order and let $P_1(K)$ denote scalar polynomials of total degree at most one. For an ordered edge $[i,j]$, put $\\phi_{ij}=\\lambda_i\\nabla\\lambda_j-\\lambda_j\\nabla\\lambda_i$; reversing its orientation changes the sign. Set\n$$W_h^0:=\\{q\\in C^0(\\overline\\Omega):q|_K\\in P_1(K)\\text{ for every }K\\in\\mathcal T\\}.$$\nThe first-family lowest-order Nedelec space is\n$$N_h^1:=\\{u\\in H(\\operatorname{curl};\\Omega):u|_K\\in\\operatorname{span}\\{\\phi_{ij}:0\\le i<j\\le3\\}\\text{ for every }K\\in\\mathcal T,\\text{ and every global edge }e\\text{ has one common oriented circulation }\\int_e u|_K\\cdot t_e\\,ds\\text{ for all }K\\supset e\\}.$$\nThe local Raviart–Thomas space is $RT_0(K)=\\{a+c x:a\\in\\mathbb R^3,\\ c\\in\\mathbb R\\}$. With $H(\\operatorname{div};\\Omega)$ as defined by [[def-na-hdiv-space]], set\n$$N_h^2:=\\{v\\in H(\\operatorname{div};\\Omega):v|_K\\in RT_0(K)\\text{ for every }K\\in\\mathcal T,\\text{ and every global face }F\\text{ has one common oriented flux }\\int_F v|_K\\cdot n_F\\,dS\\text{ for all }K\\supset F\\},\\qquad N_h^3:=\\{q\\in L^2(\\Omega):q|_K\\text{ is constant for every }K\\in\\mathcal T\\}.$$\nThe covariant affine Piola map for $N_h^1$ and contravariant affine Piola map for $N_