      "description": "{\"scope\": \"Define weak incompressible Navier–Stokes on bounded Lipschitz domains in d=2,3 with viscosity nu>0, homogeneous Dirichlet data and pressure gauge. Use NA34's actual stable mini-element pair and a skew-symmetric convective form. Reuse existing finite-dimensional Brouwer; prove existence of a backward-Euler finite-dimensional discrete solution, discrete energy inequality and subsequential convergence to a weak solution for a specified mesh/time family; uniqueness is conditional in 3D. Prove a velocity/pressure error bound only on a supplied sufficiently smooth exact solution interval, with explicit norms and nu-dependent constants. Do not assert Reynolds-uniform robustness from an ordinary Gronwall estimate.\", \"proof_route\": \"Brouwer fixed-point existence using the discrete energy outward-pointing bound and existing `thm-brouwer-fixed-point-theorem` (prove only the outward-pointing-zero corollary); derive skew cancellation, pressure cancellation and energy. Prove discrete Sobolev and trilinear bounds by NA28 scaling/root Sobolev. Use PE12 time-translate compactness for strong L2 velocity and pass convection; derive divergence/initial trace and weak energy lower semicontinuity. Smooth errors use approximation, discrete inf-sup and Gronwall.\", \"examples\": \"2D Taylor–Green manufactured flow, energy budget, pressure gauge, unresolved 3D turbulence as a conditional computation.\"}",
