    "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $0<T<\\infty$, let $H$ be a separable real Hilbert space, let $X\\subseteq H$ be a dense real linear subspace, and let $u_0\\in H$. Suppose $u\\in L^2(0,T;H)$ and $\\|u(t)\\|_H\\le M$ for almost every $t$, for some finite $M$. Suppose also that for every $v\\in X$ there is $h_v\\in L^1(0,T)$ such that, for every $\\eta\\in C^1([0,T])$ vanishing near $T$,\n$$-\\int_0^T (u(t),v)_H\\eta'(t)\\,dt=\\int_0^T h_v(t)\\eta(t)\\,dt+(u_0,v)_H\\eta(0).$$\nThen there is a unique weakly continuous map $\\widetilde u:[0,T]\\to H$ equal to $u$ almost everywhere and satisfying $\\widetilde u(0)=u_0$. Here weak continuity means that $t\\mapsto(\\widetilde u(t),w)_H$ is continuous for every $w\\in H$.",
