    "statement": "Let $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a bounded connected Lipschitz domain with $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$, and let $V=H^1_0(D;\\mathbb R^d)$ as in [[def-na-stokes-zero-mean-pressure-and-velocity-spaces]]. For $a,b,c\\in V$, define the real **skew convective form**\n$$c(a;b,c):=\\frac12\\int_D\\big((a\\cdot\\nabla)b\\cdot c-(a\\cdot\\nabla)c\\cdot b\\big)\\,dx.$$\nThe middle and last slots are displayed separately to emphasize $c(a;b,c)=-c(a;c,b)$. In particular $c(a;b,b)=0$. The integrals are well-defined on $V$ by [[lem-na-evolutionary-skew-convective-form-bound]]. If additionally $\\operatorname{div}a=0$, then $c(a;b,c)=\\int_D(a\\cdot\\nabla)b\\cdot c$.",
