    "title": "MINI backward Euler converges subsequentially to a solenoidal energy weak velocity",
    "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$, $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$, be nonempty, bounded, connected, Lipschitz and polyhedral, and let $0<T<\\infty$. Let $\\{\\mathcal T_j\\}$ be matching shape-regular affine simplicial meshes with $h_j\\to0$, and let the time partitions of $[0,T]$ have maximum step tending to zero, with no relation required between the two limits. Let $f\\in L^2(0,T;L^2(D)^d)$ and $u_0\\in H_\\sigma$. On each mesh take $u_j^0=P_{Z_j}u_0$, the $L^2$-orthogonal projection onto the weak MINI kernel, and choose any backward Euler MINI solution from [[thm-na-mini-be-step-existence-energy]]. Then a subsequence of piecewise-constant velocities converges strongly in $L^2(0,T;L^2(D)^d)$ and weakly in $L^2(0,T;H^1_0(D)^d)$ to a velocity $u$ satisfying the solenoidal weak momentum equation, initial trace and energy inequality in [[def-na-solenoidal-energy-weak-ns-velocity]]. This theorem supplies the velocity limit and its energy inequality. It does not assert the pressure regularity and pressure-bearing formulation required by the PE06 plan; the remaining pressure obligation is explicitly escalated on the A page.",
