        "nonlinear-parabolic-compactness-and-monotone-evolution"
      ],
      "description": "{\"scope\": \"Define FAS for F_h(u_h)=f_h with iterate restriction I_h^H, residual restriction R_h^H, prolongation P_H^h, coarse operator F_H and tau correction; specify nonlinear pre/post smoothing and finite budgets/branch failure. Prove fine-root fixed-point consistency for arbitrary consistent transfers when the coarse right side is F_H(Iu)+R(f-F_h(u)); require the coarse solver return the selected root Iu at zero defect. Prove exact reduction to linear correction multigrid when operators/smoothers/coarse solves are linear. Prove local convergence near a root from a bound q<1 on the derivative of the actual FAS cycle plus a proved Lipschitz derivative bound and invariant radius. Give a semilinear monotone diffusion example with actually verified smooth branch/smoother/coarse assumptions. Mesh-independent basin/rate requires those constants uniformly in h; no arbitrary nonlinear FAS convergence claim.\", \"proof_route\": \"Substitute the exact root and telescope the coarse correction. Differentiate every smoother, restriction, implicit coarse branch and prolongation at the root; use the local implicit theorem for the coarse Jacobian inverse and derive the linearized two-grid error operator exactly. NA07 contraction applies only when this derivative equals a linear cycle satisfying its actual smoothing/approximation hypotheses. Mean-value integral yields ||E(u)-u*||≤(q+Lr/2)||u-u*|| on the stated ball; choose r with q+Lr/2<1, prove invariance and iteration contraction. Coarse inexact solves add a quantified residual-to-correction defect with its own inverse bound. Cost recurrence includes nonlinear smoothing/coarse work, not a blanket O(N).\", \"examples\": \"nonlinear reaction Poisson tau cancellation, zero-tau inconsistent fixed point, linear FAS equivalence, loss of local basin near a bifurcation.\"}",
