        {
          "id": "def-scaled-symmetric-compact-kernel-family",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Scaled symmetric compactly supported kernel family",
          "statement": "Fix an integer $d\\ge1$. An **admissible smoothing kernel** is a radial function $W\\in C_c^2(\\mathbb R^d,[0,\\infty))$, supported in the closed Euclidean ball $\\overline B(0,R)$ of some radius $R>0$ ([[def-metric-ball]]), with $\\int_{\\mathbb R^d}W(z)\\,dz=1$. Here radial means $W(z)=w(|z|)$ for some function $w:[0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$, and $C_c^2$ means twice continuously differentiable with compact support. All vector norms are the Euclidean norm from [[def-euclidean-inner-product]], and $\\|D^2W\\|_\\infty$ uses the induced operator norm. Throughout this pair, $L^\\infty$ norms are suprema of Euclidean norms, and norms of multilinear derivatives are the induced operator norms. Compactly supported integrals use [[def-support-and-compactly-supported-riemann-integral-in-rn]], where $\\operatorname{supp}f$ is the closure of the set on which $f$ is nonzero.\n\nFor $\\varepsilon>0$ define the scaled kernel $W_\\varepsilon(z)=\\varepsilon^{-d}W(z/\\varepsilon)$. Write $M_0=\\|W\\|_\\infty$, $M_1=\\|\\nabla W\\|_\\infty$, $M_2=\\|D^2W\\|_\\infty$, $m_2=\\int |z|^2W(z)\\,dz$, and $m_3=\\int |z|^3|\\nabla W(z)|\\,dz$. The norm functions and moment integrands are continuous with compact support. They are bounded and Riemann integrable on a bounding Jordan box by [[thm-continuous-functions-on-compact-jordan-sets-are-integrable]], so these constants are finite.\n\nFor continuous $f:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R$, define the full-space smoother and its kernel-gradient operator by\n$$S_\\varepsilon f(x)=\\int_{\\mathbb R^d}f(x-z)W_\\varepsilon(z)\\,dz,\\qquad D_\\varepsilon f(x)=\\int_{\\mathbb R^d}f(y)\\nabla W_\\varepsilon(x-y)\\,dy.$$\nFor each fixed $x$, both scalar integrands and every component of the vector integrand are continuous and compactly supported, hence Riemann integrable on a bounding Jordan box by [[thm-continuous-functions-on-compact-jordan-sets-are-integrable]]. Thus the displayed integrals exist as compactly supported Riemann integrals; the vector integral defining $D_\\varepsilon f$ is taken componentwise.\n\nThis page fixes $\\varepsilon$ in the finite-particle system. Limits $\\varepsilon\\to0$ are used only in the stated kernel-bias and joint-refinement results.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-euclidean-inner-product",
            "def-metric-ball",
            "def-support-and-compactly-supported-riemann-integral-in-rn",
