          "title": "Cellwise oscillation bound for particle quadrature",
          "statement": "Let g be compactly supported and Lipschitz with constant L_g, meaning |g(y)−g(x)|≤L_g|y−x|, with supp(g)⊂Ω, and use the cells and nodes of [[def-meshfree-cell-quadrature-and-fill-radius]]. Define osc_C(g)=sup_{y,z∈C}|g(y)−g(z)| and let J_g={j:C_j∩supp(g)≠∅}. Then\n\n$$\\left|\\int_\\Omega g(y)dy-Q_hg\\right|\\le\\sum_{j\\in J_g}V_j\\operatorname{osc}_{C_j}(g)\\le 2hL_g\\sum_{j\\in J_g}V_j.$$",
