      "description": "{\"scope\": \"genuinely-new integral-equation discretization guarantees\\n\\nA: `nystrom-product-integration-and-fredholm-error`.\\n\\nOn X=C([a,b]), define K u(x)=integral k(x,y)u(y)dy, smooth continuous-kernel Nyström with specified quadrature and reconstructed K_n, and product integration k(x,y)=s(x,y)a(x,y) with a specified weak singularity s and exact/computably enclosed product weights. The equations are (I-K)u=f and (I-K_n)u_n=f_n. In the operator-norm route prove ||K-K_n||<=epsilon_n in the stated X/operator spaces; if ||(I-K)^-1|| epsilon_n<1, derive discrete inverse bound and ||u-u_n|| <= ||(I-K_n)^-1|| (||f-f_n||+||(K-K_n)u||). **Do not assert norm convergence on C for arbitrary point-sampling quadrature**: standard Nyström commonly needs the collectively compact route. Prove pointwise consistency and collective compactness (uniform boundedness/equicontinuity), then uniform discrete invertibility from contradiction/compact subsequences and continuous injectivity. Error rate uses quadrature of k(x,.)u(.), with its actual regularity, not all continuous unit-ball functions. Include a singular-kernel product-integration instance with weight stability and consistency proved, not assumed.\\n\\nSame-frontier PC-NYST suppliers: collectively compact approximation theorem, reconstruction/grid equivalence, weight stability, singular-kernel truncation/compactness for the selected exponents. Canonical Fredholm alternative explicitly assumes AC; carry it if using that proof route. Canonical integral-operator compactness/Arzelà–Ascoli are candidate suppliers to inspect; any mismatching interface gets a local proof here. Eigenvalue/resonance approximation additionally needs isolated spectral-cluster multiplicity proof, assigned PC-NYST before PC-SCAT consumers. B: smooth separable kernel exact finite-rank solve; nearly singular resolvent amplifies quadrature error; weak singularity lowering order; standard Nyström not norm-convergent on all C unit-ball inputs. Source: Atkinson The Numerical Solution of Integral Equations of the Second Kind https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511626340 ; Anselone Collectively Compact Operator Approximation Theory https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4613-9116-3 . Reading pending.\", \"proof_route\": [\"On X=C([a,b]), define K u(x)=integral k(x,y)u(y)dy, smooth continuous-kernel Nyström with specified quadrature and reconstructed K_n, and product integration k(x,y)=s(x,y)a(x,y) with a specified weak singularity s and exact/computably enclosed product weights. The equations are (I-K)u=f and (I-K_n)u_n=f_n. In the operator-norm route prove ||K-K_n||<=epsilon_n in the stated X/operator spaces; if ||(I-K)^-1|| epsilon_n<1, derive discrete inverse bound and ||u-u_n|| <= ||(I-K_n)^-1|| (||f-f_n||+||(K-K_n)u||). **Do not assert norm convergence on C for arbitrary point-sampling quadrature**: standard Nyström commonly needs the collectively compact route. Prove pointwise consistency and collective compactness (uniform boundedness/equicontinuity), then uniform discrete invertibility from contradiction/compact subsequences and continuous injectivity. Error rate uses quadrature of k(x,.)u(.), with its actual regularity, not all continuous unit-ball functions. Include a singular-kernel product-integration instance with weight stability and consistency proved, not assumed.\", \"Same-frontier PC-NYST suppliers: collectively compact approximation theorem, reconstruction/grid equivalence, weight stability, singular-kernel truncation/compactness for the selected exponents. Canonical Fredholm alternative explicitly assumes AC; carry it if using that proof route. Canonical integral-operator compactness/Arzelà–Ascoli are candidate suppliers to inspect; any mismatching interface gets a local proof here. Eigenvalue/resonance approximation additionally needs isolated spectral-cluster multiplicity proof, assigned PC-NYST before PC-SCAT consumers. B: smooth separable kernel exact finite-rank solve; nearly singular resolvent amplifies quadrature error; weak singularity lowering order; standard Nyström not norm-convergent on all C unit-ball inputs. Source: Atkinson The Numerical Solution of Integral Equations of the Second Kind https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511626340 ; Anselone Collectively Compact Operator Approximation Theory https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4613-9116-3 . Reading pending.\"], \"examples\": \"smooth separable kernel exact finite-rank solve; nearly singular resolvent amplifies quadrature error; weak singularity lowering order; standard Nyström not norm-convergent on all C unit-ball inputs.\"}",
