      "description": "{\"scope\": \"Define a concrete first-order incremental pressure-correction algorithm with explicit predictor, discrete projection, pressure update and boundary conditions; prove mass-inner-product projection and a matching energy estimate. Prove first-order velocity accuracy on the precise periodic smooth-data branch first; bounded-domain pressure and boundary-layer rates require separate hypotheses and proofs. Define rotational/second-order variants without claiming their rates until individually proved. Include block factorization and pressure Schur-complement preconditioners, proving spectral equivalence only from NA34 inf-sup/coercivity plus specified mass/stiffness scalings; this result supplies actual solver estimates, not generic improvement.\", \"proof_route\": \"Orthogonal decomposition and pressure increment square identity; derive splitting error equation, retain artificial pressure boundary term, estimate in appropriate dual norms, then time Gronwall. Periodicity removes the boundary defect only in that theorem. Reuse `def-block-lu-factorisation` and `thm-block-lu-factorisation-via-an-invertible-leading-block`; derive only the PDE Schur energy identity and uniform spectral bounds; bound supremum quotient with inf-sup. No pressure Poisson solve silently imposes physical pressure data.\", \"examples\": \"periodic projection, wall pressure boundary artifact, block preconditioner eigenvalues, checkerboard mode.\"}",
