  {
    "id": "lem-pe26-preconditioned-operator-norm-bound",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "Eigenvalue bounds from a left-inverse preconditioner",
    "deps": [],
    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 0,
    "statement": "Let $A:V\\to V'$ be symmetric positive definite on a finite-dimensional real vector space, and let $L:V\\to U$, $T:U\\to V$ satisfy $LT=I_U$. Every eigenvalue of\n\n$$G=(LA^{-1}L^T)(T^TAT)$$\n\nlies in $[1,\\|TL\\|_A^2]$, where $\\|Q\\|_A:=\\sup_{v\\ne0}\\sqrt{\\langle A Qv,Qv\\rangle/\\langle Av,v\\rangle}$. When $V=\\{0\\}$, set $\\|Q\\|_A=0$ for its unique endomorphism. In that case $LT=I_U$ forces $U=\\{0\\}$, the spectrum of $G$ is empty, and the eigenvalue assertion is vacuous.",
    "source_path": "items/lem-pe26-preconditioned-operator-norm-bound.md",
    "provenance": {
