  {
    "id": "def-pe26-discrete-harmonic-extension-and-schur-complement",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Discrete harmonic extension and interface Schur complement",
    "deps": [
      "def-pe26-scalar-substructuring-model",
      "def-pe26-primal-interface-spaces-and-jumps",
      "thm-pe26-local-energy-kernel-and-interior-spd",
      "def-block-lu-factorisation",
      "thm-block-lu-factorisation-via-an-invertible-leading-block"
    ],
    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 2,
    "statement": "Use the interior/interface ordering of [[def-pe26-scalar-substructuring-model]]. The boundary-trace spaces $W_i$, $W=\\prod_iW_i$, the conforming space $\\widehat W$, the partially assembled space $\\widetilde W$, and the inclusion $R:\\widehat W\\to W$ are those of [[def-pe26-primal-interface-spaces-and-jumps]]. In particular, $R$ identifies the copies of a conforming interface trace. In subdomain $i$, write its stiffness matrix as\n\n$$K_i=\\begin{pmatrix}K_{II}^{(i)}&K_{I\\Gamma}^{(i)}\\\\K_{\\Gamma I}^{(i)}&K_{\\Gamma\\Gamma}^{(i)}\\end{pmatrix}.$$\n\nBy [[thm-pe26-local-energy-kernel-and-interior-spd]], $K_{II}^{(i)}$ is positive definite when nonempty; on the zero-dimensional interior space its unique endomorphism is invertible. For admissible boundary trace $g_i$, the **discrete harmonic extension** is\n\n$$H_i g_i:=\\begin{pmatrix}-(K_{II}^{(i)})^{-1}K_{I\\Gamma}^{(i)}g_i\\\\g_i\\end{pmatrix}.$$\n\nThe local **interface Schur complement** is\n\n$$S_i:=K_{\\Gamma\\Gamma}^{(i)}-K_{\\Gamma I}^{(i)}(K_{II}^{(i)})^{-1}K_{I\\Gamma}^{(i)}.$$\n\nThis is the Schur complement in [[def-block-lu-factorisation]]. The local Schur form on a trace is $g_i^TS_i g_i$. The block identity and the associated block LU factorization use [[thm-block-lu-factorisation-via-an-invertible-leading-block]] with leading block $K_{II}^{(i)}$. Assembling local Schur forms on $\\widehat W$ gives $\\widehat S=R^T(\\operatorname{diag}_i S_i)R$; restricting the same block-diagonal form to $\\widetilde W$ gives the partially assembled operator $\\widetilde S$.",
    "source_path": "items/def-pe26-discrete-harmonic-extension-and-schur-complement.md",
    "provenance": {
      "statement": "literature-derived",
      "proof": "not-applicable"
    },
    "sources": {
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "Olof B. Widlund, Introduction to the Design and Theory of Domain Decomposition Algorithms, DD20 Tutorial, pp. 35–37",
          "url": "https://cs.nyu.edu/~widlund/SD_rev_tutorial.pdf"
        },
        {
          "title": "Oliver Rheinbach, Parallel Scalable Iterative Substructuring, Chapter 2, §§2.1–2.3",
          "url": "https://d-nb.info/983219192/34"
        }
      ]
    }
