    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 3,
    "statement": "Assume the hypotheses of [[def-pe26-primal-interface-spaces-and-jumps]] and the energy setting of [[thm-pe26-local-energy-kernel-and-interior-spd]]. If each floating local component has at least one primal vertex value fixed in its dual subproblem, its local dual stiffness is positive definite. If all subdomain vertices are primal and the global Dirichlet boundary is nonempty, the partially assembled interface energy is positive definite; hence the BDDC and FETI-DP exact local and coarse solves are well-defined.",
