  {
    "id": "thm-pe26-static-condensation-is-exact-interface-solve",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Static condensation is the exact interface problem",
    "deps": [
      "def-pe26-scalar-substructuring-model",
      "thm-pe26-local-energy-kernel-and-interior-spd",
      "def-pe26-discrete-harmonic-extension-and-schur-complement",
      "thm-block-lu-factorisation-via-an-invertible-leading-block"
    ],
    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 3,
    "statement": "Let $f_i=(f_I^{(i)},f_\\Gamma^{(i)})^T$ be local load contributions whose assembly is the global Galerkin load. For the global conforming Dirichlet finite-element system from [[def-pe26-scalar-substructuring-model]], eliminating all subdomain interior variables gives the assembled interface Schur system. Its solution trace is exactly the trace of the unique global Galerkin solution. After solving for this trace, reconstruct each local interior vector by\n\n$$u_I^{(i)}=(K_{II}^{(i)})^{-1}(f_I^{(i)}-K_{I\\Gamma}^{(i)}u_\\Gamma^{(i)}).$$\n\nThese interior values recover the unique global Galerkin solution; the trace-dependent homogeneous part of each local reconstruction is the discrete harmonic extension.",
    "source_path": "items/thm-pe26-static-condensation-is-exact-interface-solve.md",
    "provenance": {
      "statement": "literature-derived",
      "proof": "ai-altered"
    },
    "sources": {
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "Olof B. Widlund, Introduction to the Design and Theory of Domain Decomposition Algorithms, DD20 Tutorial, pp. 35–37",
          "url": "https://cs.nyu.edu/~widlund/SD_rev_tutorial.pdf"
        },
        {
          "title": "Jan Mandel and Bedřich Sousedík, BDDC and FETI-DP under Minimalist Assumptions, §5",
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0708.4031"
        }
      ]
    }
