  {
    "id": "def-pe26-scaled-averaging-and-bddc-preconditioner",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Coefficient-scaled averaging and BDDC",
    "deps": [
      "def-pe26-primal-interface-spaces-and-jumps",
      "def-pe26-discrete-harmonic-extension-and-schur-complement",
      "thm-pe26-primal-constraints-remove-floating-kernels"
    ],
    "justified_by": [
      "prop-pe26-bddc-constrained-local-minimization"
    ],
    "dependency_level": 4,
    "statement": "Use the spaces and partial Schur operator of [[def-pe26-primal-interface-spaces-and-jumps]] and [[def-pe26-discrete-harmonic-extension-and-schur-complement]]. Let $E_0:\\widetilde W\\to\\widehat W$ average every remaining interface degree of freedom and preserve every already-shared primal value. It is a scaled average if the weights for all copies of each such degree of freedom sum to one. Put $\\bar E:=R E_0:\\widetilde W\\to\\widetilde W$. Then $E_0R=I_{\\widehat W}$ and $\\bar E$ is a projection onto $\\widehat W$.\n\nIn the PE26 two-dimensional corner-constraint branch, each non-primal node is interior to one interface edge shared by exactly two subdomains $i,j$. Set\n\n$$ (E_0w)(x)=\\frac{\\rho_i}{\\rho_i+\\rho_j}w_i(x)+\\frac{\\rho_j}{\\rho_i+\\rho_j}w_j(x). $$\n\nAt primal nodes the copies already agree, so the average is the common value. For any finite-dimensional positive definite partial Schur operator $\\widetilde S$, the **BDDC preconditioner** is\n\n$$M_{\\rm BDDC}^{-1}:=E_0\\widetilde S^{-1}E_0^T:\\widehat W'\\to\\widehat W,$$\n\nfor the assembled interface system with operator $\\widehat S=R^T\\widetilde S R$. Its constrained partial-energy interpretation is established in [[prop-pe26-bddc-constrained-local-minimization]].",
    "source_path": "items/def-pe26-scaled-averaging-and-bddc-preconditioner.md",
    "provenance": {
      "statement": "literature-derived",
      "proof": "not-applicable"
    },
    "sources": {
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "Olof B. Widlund, Introduction to the Design and Theory of Domain Decomposition Algorithms, DD20 Tutorial, pp. 87–90 and 96–97",
          "url": "https://cs.nyu.edu/~widlund/SD_rev_tutorial.pdf"
        },
        {
          "title": "Jan Mandel and Bedřich Sousedík, BDDC and FETI-DP under Minimalist Assumptions, §§3.1–3.2",
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0708.4031"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "lem-pe26-discrete-trace-schur-equivalence",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "Discrete Schur energy and the fractional trace norm",
    "deps": [
      "def-pe26-scalar-substructuring-model",
      "def-pe26-discrete-harmonic-extension-and-schur-complement",
      "thm-pe26-harmonic-extension-minimizes-energy"
    ],
    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 4,
    "statement": "Let $\\Omega_i$ be one of the shape-regular polygonal subdomains in [[def-pe26-scalar-substructuring-model]], with a matching quasiuniform $P_1$ mesh. For any continuous piecewise-linear boundary trace $g$, let $S_i^{\\rm fl}$ be the Schur complement of the floating local stiffness matrix, before outer Dirichlet values are fixed, formed by the same interior elimination as in [[def-pe26-discrete-harmonic-extension-and-schur-complement]]. Define\n\n$$|g|_{1/2,\\partial\\Omega_i}^2:=\\int_{\\partial\\Omega_i}\\int_{\\partial\\Omega_i}\\frac{|g(s)-g(t)|^2}{|s-t|^2}\\,ds\\,dt.$$\n\nThis seminorm is taken modulo constants. The floating local Schur energy satisfies\n\n$$c\\rho_i|g|_{1/2,\\partial\\Omega_i}^2\\le g^TS_i^{\\rm fl} g\\le C\\rho_i|g|_{1/2,\\partial\\Omega_i}^2,$$\n\nwhere $c,C>0$ depend only on the fixed scaled polygon-shape parameters (including boundary-chart and mean-zero Poincaré bounds), mesh shape-regularity and quasiuniformity. The upper bound is realized by a boundary-preserving finite-element lifting; the minimum-energy lifting is the floating discrete harmonic extension. For an admissible trace $g$, whose outer Dirichlet values are zero, $g^TS_i^{\\rm fl}g=g^TS_i g$ for the Dirichlet-restricted Schur matrix of [[def-pe26-discrete-harmonic-extension-and-schur-complement]], so the same inequalities hold for that matrix on its domain.",
    "source_path": "items/lem-pe26-discrete-trace-schur-equivalence.md",
    "provenance": {
      "statement": "literature-derived",
      "proof": "ai-altered"
    },
    "sources": {
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "Olof B. Widlund, Introduction to the Design and Theory of Domain Decomposition Algorithms, DD20 Tutorial, pp. 24–26",
          "url": "https://cs.nyu.edu/~widlund/SD_rev_tutorial.pdf"
        },
        {
          "title": "Oliver Rheinbach, Parallel Scalable Iterative Substructuring, Chapter 1 §1.7 and Chapter 2 §2.4",
          "url": "https://d-nb.info/983219192/34"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "prop-pe26-bddc-constrained-local-minimization",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "title": "BDDC is the constrained partial-energy minimizer",
    "deps": [
      "def-pe26-scaled-averaging-and-bddc-preconditioner",
      "thm-pe26-primal-constraints-remove-floating-kernels"
    ],
    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 5,
    "statement": "For every assembled residual $f\\in\\widehat W'$, the unique minimizer over $w\\in\\widetilde W$ of\n\n$$J_f(w)=\\tfrac12\\langle\\widetilde S w,w\\rangle-\\langle f,E_0w\\rangle$$\n\nis $w_* = \\widetilde S^{-1}E_0^T f$. The conforming correction returned by BDDC is $E_0 w_*=E_0\\widetilde S^{-1}E_0^T f$.",
    "source_path": "items/prop-pe26-bddc-constrained-local-minimization.md",
    "provenance": {
