    "dependency_level": 5,
    "statement": "Use $\\widetilde W$, $\\widehat W$, $E_0$, $R$, $B$ and $\\Lambda=\\operatorname{range}B$ as defined in [[def-pe26-primal-interface-spaces-and-jumps]] and [[def-pe26-scaled-averaging-and-bddc-preconditioner]]. Assume that $\\widetilde S:\\widetilde W\\to\\widetilde W'$ is symmetric positive definite. In the PE26 corner branch this follows from [[thm-pe26-primal-constraints-remove-floating-kernels]] when all subdomain vertices are primal and the global Dirichlet boundary is nonempty; for other primal choices it is a separate admissibility requirement. Use the inherited Euclidean inner product to identify $\\Lambda$ with $\\Lambda'$ in the transpose and coordinate formulas below. Regard $\\bar E=R E_0$ as a projection on $\\widetilde W$. Since $\\ker B=\\operatorname{range}\\bar E=\\widehat W$, each class of traces with the same jump has a unique representative in $\\ker\\bar E$. Define $B_D^T:\\Lambda\\to\\widetilde W$ by assigning to $\\lambda\\in\\Lambda$ that unique representative $w$ with $Bw=\\lambda$ and $\\bar Ew=0$. This is the scaled right inverse; it obeys $BB_D^T=I_\\Lambda$ and $B_D^TB=I_{\\widetilde W}-\\bar E$. The latter identity makes the primal and dual projections complementary. In the two-subdomain edge case, its two entries are the coefficient-scaled jump weights complementary to those in $E_0$.\n\nThe **FETI-DP dual operator** and its preconditioner are\n\n$$F:=B\\widetilde S^{-1}B^T:\\Lambda\\to\\Lambda',\\qquad M_{\\rm FETI-DP}^{-1}:=B_D\\widetilde S B_D^T:\\Lambda'\\to\\Lambda.$$\n\nThe multiplier convention removes dependent row coordinates: $\\lambda$ is in $\\operatorname{range}B$, so no arbitrary multiplier component in $\\ker B^T$ is retained. Elimination of the partially assembled displacement and the resulting exact dual system are proved in [[prop-pe26-feti-dp-is-dual-schur-complement]].",
