    },
    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\Omega$ have a finite matching affine simplicial mesh $\\mathcal T_h$ as in [[def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes]], and let $H^1_0(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)=W^{1,2}_0(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$ have the closure convention of [[def-wkp-zero-as-a-sobolev-closure]] and [[def-hk-and-hk-zero-notation]]. For every boundary facet $F\\subset\\partial K$ there is a bounded affine-simplex trace map $T_{K,F}:W^{1,2}(K;\\mathbb R)\\to L^2(F;\\mathbb R)$ agreeing with classical restriction on smooth functions. If $w\\in H^1_0(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$, then $T_{K,F}(w|_K)=0$ in $L^2(F;\\mathbb R)$. In particular, any globally $H^1(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$ function that is polynomial on each cell and belongs to $H^1_0(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$ has zero classical boundary restriction on every boundary facet."
  },
