    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Fix $d\\ge2$, a degree $k\\ge1$, and a shape-regular matching affine simplicial mesh family as in [[def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes]]. There is a selected constant $1\\le C_{\\mathrm{tr}}<\\infty$, depending only on $d,k$ and the shape-regularity bound, such that for every cell $K$, every facet $F\\subset\\partial K$, and every scalar $v_h|_K\\in\\mathbb P_k(K)$,\n$$h_F\\|\\partial_{n_{K,F}}v_h\\|_{L^2(F)}^2\\le C_{\\mathrm{tr}}^2\\|\\nabla v_h\\|_{L^2(K)}^2,$$\nwhere $h_F=|K|/|F|$ and $n_{K,F}$ is the outward unit normal of $K$ on $F$."
