    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $K\\subset\\mathbb R^d$, $d\\ge2$, be a nondegenerate affine simplex, let $F$ be one of its facets, and let $s>1/2$. Restriction of smooth functions has a unique bounded extension\n$$T_F:H^s(K)\\longrightarrow L^2(F),\\qquad \\|T_Fv\\|_{L^2(F)}\\le C_s\\|v\\|_{H^s(K)},$$\nwhere $H^s(K)$ is the restriction space of [[def-nitsche-restriction-bessel-potential-sobolev-spaces]]. The constant depends only on $s$ and the Fourier normalization, not on the location or orientation of the supporting hyperplane. If $V\\in H^s(\\mathbb R^d)$ is an extension of $v$, then $T_Fv$ is the restriction to $F$ of the unique $L^2$ hyperplane trace of $V$; hence it is independent of the chosen extension."
