    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\ge2$, let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected polyhedral open set, and let $\\mathcal T_h$ be a finite matching affine simplicial mesh of $\\Omega$ as in [[def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes]]. Fix a polynomial degree $k\\ge1$. Let $V_h$ be the real scalar conforming polynomial space of [[def-broken-and-conforming-polynomial-spaces]], viewed as a subspace of $H^1(\\Omega)$ by [[thm-matching-continuous-piecewise-polynomials-are-wkp]], and let $Y_h:=V_h\\cap H^1_0(\\Omega)$, where $H^1_0$ is the closure convention of [[def-wkp-zero-as-a-sobolev-closure]]; [[lem-nitsche-h-one-zero-functions-have-zero-facet-traces]] proves its facet-trace consequence. Boundary facets form $\\mathcal F_h^\\partial$. If $F\\in\\mathcal F_h^\\partial$, let $K_F$ be its unique incident cell, $n_F$ its outward unit normal, $|F|$ its $(d-1)$-dimensional measure, and set $h_F:=|K_F|/|F|>0$. For functions with a defined boundary normal trace write $\\partial_n v:=\\nabla v\\cdot n_F$ on $F$.\n\nLet $\\mathcal X_h$ consist of $v\\in H^1(\\Omega)$ such that for every cell $K$ there is $s_K>1/2$ with $v|_K\\in H^{1+s_K}(K)$. By [[lem-nitsche-fractional-face-trace-on-simplex]], $v$ has an $L^2(F)$ trace on each facet, and each component of $\\nabla(v|_K)$ is in $H^{s_K}(K)$, hence has an $L^2(F)$ trace by the same lemma; the derivative mapping follows from $|\\xi_j|\\langle\\xi\\rangle^{s_K}\\le\\langle\\xi\\rangle^{1+s_K}$ in the Bessel-potential norm. Thus $\\partial_n v$ and all displayed integrals are defined. In particular, $V_h\\subseteq\\mathcal X_h$ and the exact/adjoint functions in the later regularity hypotheses lie in $\\mathcal X_h$. For a dimensionless penalty coefficient $\\gamma_0\\ge0$ and symmetry parameter $\\theta\\in\\{0,1\\}$, define the same bilinear formula on $\\mathcal X_h\\times\\mathcal X_h$:\n$$a_h^\\theta(v,w):=\\int_\\Omega\\nabla v\\cdot\\nabla w\\,dx-\\sum_{F\\in\\mathcal F_h^\\partial}\