          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\ge2$, let $\\widehat S_d$ be the reference simplex, and let $F_K(\\widehat x)=b+B\\widehat x$ map $\\overline{\\widehat S_d}$ affinely onto a nondegenerate closed simplex $K$, with $\\det B>0$. Sobolev spaces on $K$ mean spaces on its open interior. For every scalar $u\\in W^{1,2}(K)$ and vector field $G\\in W^{1,2}(K;\\mathbb R^d)$, each physical facet has bounded $L^2$ traces $\\gamma_Fu$ and $\\gamma_FG$, obtained by affine transfer from the reference trace maps. These traces are independent of the chosen orientation-preserving reference map, and they satisfy\n$$\\int_K u\\,\\operatorname{div}G+\\nabla u\\cdot G\\,dx=\\sum_{F\\subset\\partial K}\\int_F(\\gamma_Fu)(\\gamma_FG)\\cdot n_{K,F}\\,dS,$$\nwhere $n_{K,F}$ is the outward unit normal."
