    "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice for the weak elliptic existence suppliers used to instantiate either model branch.\n\nLet $(\\mathcal T_k,U_k)$ be generated by exact P1 Galerkin solves and the three-generation algorithm with $\\theta_E,\\theta_O\\in(0,1]$, and assume every per-call bisection budget is sufficient for a complete refinement. For the estimator and oscillation of [[def-afem-p1-residual-estimator-and-data-oscillation]], write $e_k=\\|\\nabla(u-U_k)\\|_2$, $\\eta_k=\\eta(U_k,\\mathcal T_k)$ and $\\operatorname{osc}_k=\\operatorname{osc}(U_k,\\mathcal T_k)$. On the symmetric branch $b=0$, no initial-mesh smallness is needed. On the constant-convection branch assume the uniform dual-pickup bound of [[lem-afem-convection-quasi-orthogonality-under-fine-mesh]] and set $\\mu=C_Dh_0^s|b|$. Define\n$$\\kappa=\\min\\left\\{\\frac12,\\frac{\\theta_E}{C_{\\rm eff}C_{\\rm rel}}\\right\\},\\qquad \\nu=\\begin{cases}0,&b=0,\\\\ \\mu/(1-\\mu),&b\\ne0.\\end{cases}$$\nIn the convection branch assume $\\mu<1$, so that $\\nu$ is defined and the quasi-orthogonality estimate applies, and assume $\\nu<\\kappa$. Then there are $\\beta>0$ and $0<\\alpha<1$, depending only on the displayed constants and marking parameters, such that\n$$e_{k+1}^2+\\beta\\operatorname{osc}_{k+1}^2 \\le\\alpha\\big(e_k^2+\\beta\\operatorname{osc}_{k}^2\\big).$$\n\nMoreover, after possibly reducing a positive weight $\\sigma$, there are $\\beta'>0$ and $0<\\alpha'<1$ such that\n$$e_{k+1}^2+\\beta'\\operatorname{osc}_{k+1}^2+\\sigma\\eta_{k+1}^2 \\le\\alpha'\\big(e_k^2+\\beta'\\operatorname{osc}_{k}^2+\\sigma\\eta_k^2\\big).$$\nThis second assertion records the residual-estimator reduction as part of the usual AFEM quasi-error. Constants and smallness hypotheses belong to the chosen marking and the stated dual-pickup bound.",
