      "id": "volume-integral-scattering-and-partial-wave-error-examples",
      "kind": "B",
      "category": "numerical-pdes-and-spatial-discretization",
      "label": "PC-SCAT-B",
      "title": "Volume integral scattering and partial wave error — Examples",
      "companion": "volume-integral-scattering-and-partial-wave-error",
      "requires": [
        "volume-integral-scattering-and-partial-wave-error"
      ],
      "description": "{\"scope\": \"genuinely-new volume scattering computation\\n\\nA: `volume-integral-scattering-and-partial-wave-error`.\\n\\nFor bounded D in R³ and supplied bounded compactly supported q, define K_k u(x)=integral_D exp(ik|x-y|)/(4pi|x-y|) q(y)u(y)dy on a declared L² or continuous space, k real fixed. Prove boundedness and compactness by truncating the singularity, estimating the discarded small-ball kernel by Schur bounds, and compact approximation of the remaining continuous kernel. For ||K_k||<1 prove Born/Neumann truncation error <=||K_k||^(m+1)||f||/(1-||K_k||). Otherwise existence/stability requires injectivity plus Fredholm (or PDE-owner actual scattering uniqueness under stated q/sign/radiation assumptions). Discretize using PC-NYST-compatible singular product/volume quadrature and prove far-field functional error from the solution estimate and quadrature error. For radial inputs derive the partial-wave radial BVP by explicit spherical harmonic expansion, regular-origin boundary conditions, outer matching and angular-mode truncation bound under a stated coefficient/analyticity regime. Resonance detection uses isolated complex-pole/operator analytic-Fredholm proofs only if fully supplied; a determinant nearly zero is diagnostic, not a theorem.\\n\\nPC-SCAT owns kernel compactness, volume/far-field maps, radial transform/error; PC-NYST owns discretization spectral clusters; PDE owner owns outgoing uniqueness when actually consumed; linear owner singular quadrature/special transforms; PC-SFUN supplies scaled spherical Bessel evaluations. B: small-norm scatterer Born error; near-resonant amplification; radial square-well comparison with exact matching; forward angular truncation failure at high k unless resolution grows. Sources: Colton–Kress Inverse Acoustic and Electromagnetic Scattering Theory https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-30351-8 ; Kress Linear Integral Equations https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4614-9593-2 . Reading pending. No unconditional physical scattering model claim.\", \"proof_route\": [\"For bounded D in R³ and supplied bounded compactly supported q, define K_k u(x)=integral_D exp(ik|x-y|)/(4pi|x-y|) q(y)u(y)dy on a declared L² or continuous space, k real fixed. Prove boundedness and compactness by truncating the singularity, estimating the discarded small-ball kernel by Schur bounds, and compact approximation of the remaining continuous kernel. For ||K_k||<1 prove Born/Neumann truncation error <=||K_k||^(m+1)||f||/(1-||K_k||). Otherwise existence/stability requires injectivity plus Fredholm (or PDE-owner actual scattering uniqueness under stated q/sign/radiation assumptions). Discretize using PC-NYST-compatible singular product/volume quadrature and prove far-field functional error from the solution estimate and quadrature error. For radial inputs derive the partial-wave radial BVP by explicit spherical harmonic expansion, regular-origin boundary conditions, outer matching and angular-mode truncation bound under a stated coefficient/analyticity regime. Resonance detection uses isolated complex-pole/operator analytic-Fredholm proofs only if fully supplied; a determinant nearly zero is diagnostic, not a theorem.\"], \"examples\": \"small-norm scatterer Born error; near-resonant amplification; radial square-well comparison with exact matching; forward angular truncation failure at high k unless resolution grows.\"}",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-forward-plane-wave-fixed-partial-wave-cutoff-fails",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "A fixed partial-wave cutoff misses the forward high-frequency plane wave",
          "deps": [
