            "thm-c-one-change-of-variables-for-nonnegative-lebesgue-measurable-functions",
            "thm-linear-change-of-variables-for-lebesgue-measure",
            "thm-complex-exponential-is-entire-with-derivative-itself",
            "cor-complex-exponential-cartesian-form-modulus-and-eulers-identity"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "source_path": "items/ex-forward-plane-wave-fixed-partial-wave-cutoff-fails.md",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and Dependent Choice. For a fixed direction $d\\in S^2$, consider the incident plane wave $g_k(\\omega)=e^{ikd\\cdot\\omega}$ on the unit sphere. Let $\\Pi_L$ denote projection onto degrees $0,\\ldots,L$. For each fixed $L$, its value at the forward direction tends to zero as $k\\to\\infty$, whereas $g_k(d)=e^{ik}$ has modulus one. Thus a fixed angular cutoff has forward error tending to one; uniform high-frequency accuracy below one requires the cutoff to tend to infinity.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "axiom_use": "Countable Choice and Dependent Choice are carried from the harmonic supplier used for the projection kernel; the decay bound itself is finite integration by parts.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Pierre Capel, Introduction to Scattering Theory, TALENT lecture notes",
                "url": "https://indico.mitp.uni-mainz.de/event/279/sessions/1001/attachments/2951/3418/Capel1TALENTFB22ho.pdf",
                "locator": "PDF pp. 17–21, plane-wave partial-wave decomposition; the fixed-cutoff forward-error conclusion is proved locally."
