  {
    "id": "def-supg-general-convection-diffusion-reaction-model",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Stationary multidimensional convection–diffusion–reaction P1 model",
    "deps": [
      "def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes"
    ],
    "statement": "Fix $d\\ge2$ and a bounded connected polyhedral open set $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$. Let $\\{\\mathcal T_h\\}$ be a shape-regular family of finite matching affine simplicial meshes in the sense of [[def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes]]: one finite constant $\\sigma$ satisfies $h_K/\\rho_K\\le\\sigma$ for every cell of every mesh. Put $h=\\max_{K\\in\\mathcal T_h}h_K$. Let $V_h$ be the space of continuous functions on $\\overline\\Omega$ that are affine on every cell and vanish on $\\partial\\Omega$.\n\nLet $\\epsilon>0$, $b\\in C^1(\\overline\\Omega;\\mathbb R^d)$, $c\\in C(\\overline\\Omega)$, and $f\\in C(\\overline\\Omega)$. Define $B:=\\|b\\|_{L^\\infty(\\Omega)}$ and $C:=\\|c\\|_{L^\\infty(\\Omega)}$. Assume a fixed $\\omega>0$ satisfies $c-\\frac12\\nabla\\cdot b\\ge\\omega$ on $\\Omega$. The boundary condition for this branch is $u=0$ on the whole boundary, including the inflow part $\\{x\\in\\partial\\Omega:b(x)\\cdot n(x)<0\\}$. A classical exact solution is a function $u\\in C^2(\\overline\\Omega)$ satisfying $-\\epsilon\\Delta u+b\\cdot\\nabla u+cu=f$ in $\\Omega$ and this boundary condition.",
