  {
    "id": "def-supg-one-dimensional-residual-form",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "One-dimensional residual SUPG form with the exact cell parameter",
    "deps": [
      "def-supg-one-dimensional-convection-diffusion-model"
    ],
    "statement": "Use the uniform mesh, coefficients, and spaces of [[def-supg-one-dimensional-convection-diffusion-model]]. On every cell set\n$$\\tau=\\frac{h}{2|b|}\\left(\\coth(\\mathrm{Pe})-\\frac1{\\mathrm{Pe}}\\right),\\qquad \\coth s:=\\frac{\\cosh s}{\\sinh s}.$$\nFor $w\\in S_h(g_0,g_1)+C^2([0,1])$ and $v_h\\in V_h$, define\n$$a_h(w,v_h):=\\epsilon\\int_0^1w'v_h'\\,dx+b\\int_0^1w'v_h\\,dx+\\sum_{K\\in\\mathcal T_h}\\tau\\int_K(-\\epsilon w''+bw')(bv_h')\\,dx,$$\n$$F_h(v_h):=\\int_0^1fv_h\\,dx+\\sum_{K\\in\\mathcal T_h}\\tau\\int_K f(bv_h')\\,dx.$$\nSecond derivatives are taken classically on each cell. The strong equation residual is $R_K(w):=-\\epsilon w''+bw'-f$. For P1 trial functions, $w_h''=0$ on each cell, so the cell term is $\\tau\\int_K(bw_h')(bv_h')$. On the smooth consistency extension it retains $-\\epsilon w''$; thus the full residual pairing is $\\tau\\int_K(R_K(w)+f)(bv_h')$, while the load contains the matching $f$ term. The SUPG equation is $a_h(w_h,v_h)=F_h(v_h)$ and adds the same residual-weighted streamline test perturbation to the differential equation and its load.",
