  {
    "id": "def-supg-general-residual-form",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Multidimensional P1 SUPG residual form and parameter scaling",
    "deps": [
      "def-supg-general-convection-diffusion-reaction-model"
    ],
    "statement": "Use the model and notation of [[def-supg-general-convection-diffusion-reaction-model]]. Define $s_b(K)=h_K/\\|b\\|_{L^\\infty(K)}$ when that norm is positive and $s_b(K)=+\\infty$ otherwise; define $s_c(K)=\\omega/\\|c\\|_{L^\\infty(K)}^2$ when that norm is positive and $s_c(K)=+\\infty$ otherwise. For each cell set\n$$\\delta_K:=\\theta\\min\\left\\{\\frac{h_K^2}{\\epsilon},s_b(K),s_c(K)\\right\\},\\quad 0<\\theta\\le\\frac14.$$\nThe minimum is finite and positive because its first entry is finite and positive. This scaling gives $\\delta_K\\|c\\|_{L^\\infty(K)}^2\\le\\omega/4$.\n\nFor a trial function $w$ that is the sum of a cellwise smooth function and a member of $V_h$, and $v_h\\in V_h$, define the element residual $R_K(w):=-\\epsilon\\Delta_K w+b\\cdot\\nabla w+cw$, and\n$$a_h(w,v_h):=\\epsilon(\\nabla w,\\nabla v_h)_\\Omega+(b\\cdot\\nabla w+cw,v_h)_\\Omega+\\sum_{K\\in\\mathcal T_h}\\delta_K(R_K(w),b\\cdot\\nabla v_h)_K,$$\n$$F_h(v_h):=(f,v_h)_\\Omega+\\sum_{K\\in\\mathcal T_h}\\delta_K(f,b\\cdot\\nabla v_h)_K.$$\nHere $(g_1,g_2)_D:=\\int_Dg_1g_2\\,dx$ and $\\Delta_K$ is the classical Laplacian restricted to the interior of $K$. For $w_h\\in V_h$, $\\Delta_Kw_h=0$ because $w_h$ is affine on $K$. No stability claim is part of this definition.",
