    "title": "Sound-soft exterior Helmholtz problem for a spherical obstacle",
    "deps": [],
    "dependency_level": 0,
    "statement": "Fix $a>0$, $k>0$, and $f\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb S^2;\\mathbb C)$. Write $S_a=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:|x|=a\\}$. The sound-soft exterior Helmholtz problem is to find a complex-valued $u\\in C^2(\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:|x|>a\\})$ that extends continuously to $\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:|x|\\ge a\\}$ and satisfies $(\\Delta+k^2)u=0$ for $|x|>a$, with boundary restriction $u|_{S_a}(a\\omega)=f(\\omega)$, and\n$$\\lim_{r\\to\\infty}\\sup_{\\omega\\in\\mathbb S^2}\\left|r\\bigl(\\partial_r u(r\\omega)-ik u(r\\omega)\\bigr)\\right|=0.$$\nThe time factor is $e^{-i\\omega t}$, so this is the outgoing convention. The obstacle is the closed ball $\\{|x|\\le a\\}$; its boundary is smooth and its exterior is connected. This definition makes no claim for nonspherical obstacles or nonsmooth data.",
