    "title": "Logarithmic capacity and single-layer scaling under homothety",
    "statement": "Use the logarithmic energy and capacity conventions of [[def-bem-logarithmic-capacity-and-two-dimensional-layer-scaling]]. If $K\\subset\\mathbb R^2$ is compact and has $0<\\operatorname{cap}(K)<\\infty$ and $s>0$, then $\\operatorname{cap}(sK)=s\\operatorname{cap}(K)$. If $\\Gamma$ is a closed piecewise-smooth curve and $\\lambda$ is a smooth density, define $\\Gamma_s=s\\Gamma$ and $\\lambda_s(sy)=s^{-1}\\lambda(y)$. Then\n$$V_{\\Gamma_s}\\lambda_s(sx)=V_\\Gamma\\lambda(x)-\\frac{\\log s}{2\\pi}\\int_\\Gamma\\lambda\\,ds_y.$$\nThus changing length scale adds a constant-mode term of rank at most one (zero when $s=1$); the formula is retained separately from the three-dimensional kernel $1/(4\\pi|x-y|)$.",
