    "title": "An H1-density rate for P0 single-layer Galerkin BEM",
    "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Under the mesh and coercivity hypotheses of [[thm-bem-single-layer-galerkin-wellposed-and-quasioptimal]], suppose each mesh triangle is contained in one planar face and the exact density $\\lambda\\in L^2(\\Gamma)$ is continuously differentiable on each face with $\\nabla_\\Gamma\\lambda\\in L^2(\\Gamma)$. Then the P0 Galerkin solution obeys\n$$\\|\\lambda-\\lambda_h\\|_{H^{-1/2}(\\Gamma)}\\le C h^{3/2}\\|\\nabla_\\Gamma\\lambda\\|_{L^2(\\Gamma)},$$\nwhere $C$ is independent of $h$ for a shape-regular mesh family. More generally, the same estimate holds whenever $\\lambda|_T\\in H^1(T)$ on every mesh triangle, with the gradient norm taken elementwise. No agreement of density traces across mesh edges is required.",
