    "id": "thm-bem-hypersingular-ellipticity-and-stabilized-formulation",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "The hypersingular operator is elliptic modulo constants",
    "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $W:H^{1/2}(\\Gamma)\\to H^{-1/2}(\\Gamma)$ be the hypersingular operator of [[def-bem-calderon-boundary-operators]]. It is symmetric and nonnegative, its kernel is exactly the constants, and there is $c>0$ such that\n$$\\langle W\\phi,\\phi\\rangle_\\Gamma\\ge c\\inf_{a\\in\\mathbb R}\\|\\phi-a\\|_{H^{1/2}(\\Gamma)}^2.$$\nThe real scalar $m_\\Gamma(\\phi):=\\int_\\Gamma\\phi\\,dS$ is the $L^2$ integral, not a pairing of two elements of $H^{1/2}$. The continuous embeddings $H^{1/2}\\subset L^2\\subset H^{-1/2}$ use the fixed Hilbert chart convention; the second map sends $f$ to the functional $g\\mapsto\\int_\\Gamma fg\\,dS$. Thus $m_\\Gamma(\\phi)$ can equivalently be evaluated by pairing this realized negative-order functional with $1$. The stabilized form\n$$b(\\phi,\\psi)=\\langle W\\phi,\\psi\\rangle_\\Gamma+m_\\Gamma(\\phi)m_\\Gamma(\\psi)$$\nis bounded and coercive on $H^{1/2}(\\Gamma)$. Consequently, for each $f\\in H^{-1/2}(\\Gamma)$ there is a unique $\\phi\\in H^{1/2}(\\Gamma)$ such that $b(\\phi,\\psi)=\\langle f,\\psi\\rangle_\\Gamma$ for every $\\psi\\in H^{1/2}(\\Gamma)$.",
