    "title": "Planar rotation carries H(div) normal traces to tangential traces",
    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. For a nondegenerate oriented triangle $K\\subset\\mathbb R^2$, set $R(a,b)=(-b,a)$, let $n$ be cell-outward and $t=Rn$. If $\\sigma\\in H(\\operatorname{div};K)$ is real, then $R\\sigma\\in H(\\operatorname{curl};K)$, $\\operatorname{curl}(R\\sigma)=\\operatorname{div}\\sigma$ distributionally, and $\\int_K(R\\sigma\\cdot R\\nabla\\phi+\\operatorname{curl}(R\\sigma)\\phi)=\\langle\\gamma_n\\sigma,[\\phi]\\rangle$ for all $\\phi\\in H^1(K)$. Thus weak tangential trace equals weak normal trace under $t=Rn$.\n\nHere $H(\\operatorname{curl};K):=\\{w\\in L^2(K;\\mathbb R^2):\\partial_1w_2-\\partial_2w_1\\in L^2(K)\\}$ with its graph norm. The weak tangential trace is the functional on $H^1(K)/H^1_0(K)$ defined by the integral in the Statement; the computation below proves it is the rotation of the PE08 weak normal trace.",
