      ],
      "description": "{\"scope\": \"**Exact scope.** Periodic finite electrostatic particle/mesh system with specified nonnegative deposition shape, neutralizing background, discrete Poisson solve, gather operator and leapfrog/Verlet time staggering. Reuse the actual Poisson solver; static Ewald/particle-mesh Coulomb expansion belongs to physics/chemistry audit. Prove charge deposition sums to total particle charge, zero-mode compatibility and gauge normalization. Prove the chosen deposition/gather adjoint identity under declared grid inner product; momentum or energy conservation is **scheme specific** and must be established separately. A plain staggered PIC scheme must not inherit exact energy conservation merely from adjoint gathering. Give residual-to-force error with the actual inverse/derivative norm, including mesh-dependence.\\n\\nConvergence theorem is staged: (a) time stepping error for the finite smooth particle-grid ODE, (b) force interpolation/deposition/grid-Poisson error for a fixed regularization ε and smooth compatible density, (c) particle-measure/mean-field error through XD-08, and (d) regularization-to-unregularized Vlasov–Poisson error only if separately proved on a smooth finite-time solution class. List ε-, mesh-, particle- and time-dependent constants explicitly; an ε-fixed convergence theorem is not convergence to singular Coulomb dynamics. State grid crossing/aliasing and stochastic loading effects independently.\", \"proof_route\": \"**Local suppliers.** Shape partition-of-unity and grid duality; periodic discrete Poincaré/Poisson zero-mode invertibility; residual-to-field estimate; regularized grid-force Lipschitz constant; consistency of deposition plus gather; characteristic weak formulation for regularized Vlasov; empirical measure initial error (deterministic bound or sampling theorem with dimension/rate). XD-08 supplies the stability argument, not an assumption that every empirical approximation has N^−1/2 Wasserstein error.\", \"examples\": \"**B examples.** One-dimensional periodic neutralized charge deposition; manufactured smooth density with grid error; cold two-stream model as stipulated experiment with no claimed physical validation; failure of neutrality; leapfrog energy drift versus exact semidiscrete invariant.\"}",
