        }
      ]
    },
    "statement": "On the torus and grid of [[def-periodic-pic-grid-and-inner-product]], an algebraic assignment shape is any family of functions $w_j:\\mathbb T_L^d\\to[0,\\infty)$ such that $\\sum_{j\\in J_N}w_j(x)=1$ for every $x$. For the smooth fixed-$\\varepsilon$ branch used in the force-error and ODE results, fix $\\varepsilon>0$, put $\\alpha_\\varepsilon=e^{-\\varepsilon/L}$ and choose the explicit even periodic kernel\n$$ \\eta_\\varepsilon(x)=L^{-d}\\prod_{a=1}^d \\frac{1-\\alpha_\\varepsilon^2}{1-2\\alpha_\\varepsilon\\cos(2\\pi x_a/L)+\\alpha_\\varepsilon^2}. $$ For this smooth branch and each $x\\in\\mathbb T_L^d$, set $$ Z_{\\varepsilon,h}(x)=h^d\\sum_{j\\in J_N}\\eta_\\varepsilon(x_j-x),\\qquad w_j^{\\varepsilon,h}(x)=\\frac{h^d\\eta_\\varepsilon(x_j-x)}{Z_{\\varepsilon,h}(x)}. $$ Each factor in the kernel denominator is positive, so $Z_{\\varepsilon,h}(x)>0$ and the smooth-branch weights are well-defined. For any algebraic shape family above and finitely many particle positions $X=(X_1,\\ldots,X_P)$ with charges $q_1,\\ldots,q_P\\in\\mathbb R$, write $Q=\\sum_{p=1}^Pq_p$ and define deposited charge density $$ \\rho_j(X)=h^{-d}\\sum_{p=1}^Pq_pw_j(X_p)-Q/L^d . $$\nFor any grid scalar $g$, its potential gather is $(G_Xg)_p=\\sum_jw_j(X_p)g_j$. For any grid vector $E$, its field gather is defined componentwise by the same weights, $(G_XE)_p=\\sum_jw_j(X_p)E_j$. On the smooth fixed-$\\varepsilon$ branch, $w_j$ means the explicit family $w_j^{\\varepsilon,h}$ above."
