    "statement": "Use the grid, inner product, and operator $A_h$ of [[def-periodic-pic-grid-and-inner-product]]. Then $A_h$ is self-adjoint and nonnegative, $\\ker A_h$ consists exactly of constant arrays, and $\\operatorname{ran}A_h=\\{s:\\bar s=0\\}$. Consequently, for every compatible source $\\bar s=0$, there is a unique solution $\\phi$ of $A_h\\phi=s$ with the gauge $\\bar\\phi=0$.\n\nFor $k\\in\\mathcal K_N$, the Fourier character $e_k(j)=e^{2\\pi i k\\cdot j/N}$ is an eigenvector with\n$$ \\lambda_h(k)=\\frac4{h^2}\\sum_{a=1}^d\\sin^2\\!\\left(\\frac{\\pi k_a}{N}\\right). $$\nOnly $k=0$ has eigenvalue zero."
