    "statement": "For any real grid array $s$, define its mean-zero periodic Poisson pseudoinverse by\n$$ A_h^\\dagger s:=\\text{the unique mean-zero grid array }u\\text{ such that }A_hu=s-\\bar s\\,\\mathbf1, $$\nwhere $\\bar s=L^{-d}\\langle s,\\mathbf1\\rangle_h$. This definition is well-defined by [[thm-periodic-centered-difference-poisson-zero-mode-and-gauge]]. It gives $A_hA_h^\\dagger s=s-\\bar s\\mathbf1$, $A_h^\\dagger\\mathbf1=0$, and a linear self-adjoint map on the full finite grid space."
