    "statement": "For positions $X_1,\\ldots,X_P\\in\\mathbb T_L^d$ and real charges $q_1,\\ldots,q_P$, define $Q=\\sum_pq_p$ and an admissible algebraic assignment shape $w_j$ as in [[def-periodic-pic-shape-assignment-and-gather]]. Then\n$$ h^d\\sum_{j\\in J_N}h^{-d}\\sum_{p=1}^Pq_pw_j(X_p)=Q . $$\nConsequently the neutralized source $\\rho_j(X)=h^{-d}\\sum_pq_pw_j(X_p)-Q/L^d$ has mean zero and is in the range of the periodic Poisson operator; it therefore has a unique mean-zero potential for the gauge $\\bar\\phi=0$ by [[thm-periodic-centered-difference-poisson-zero-mode-and-gauge]]."
