    "statement": "Let $\\eta_\\varepsilon$ be the explicit product kernel in [[def-periodic-pic-shape-assignment-and-gather]], with $\\alpha_\\varepsilon=e^{-\\varepsilon/L}\\in(0,1)$. Let $\\mu$ be a finite signed Borel measure on $\\mathbb T_L^d$ with mass $Q$ and total variation $\\|\\mu\\|_{\\rm TV}$. Put\n$$ \\widehat\\mu(k)=\\int_{\\mathbb T_L^d}e^{-2\\pi i k\\cdot y/L}\\,d\\mu(y),\\qquad \\kappa_k=2\\pi k/L . $$ Then $\\eta_\\varepsilon$ is strictly positive, even, smooth, and has integral one. The regularized neutralized source $$ \\rho_\\varepsilon^\\mu(x)=\\int_{\\mathbb T_L^d}\\eta_\\varepsilon(x-y)\\,d\\mu(y)-Q/L^d $$ is $C^\\infty$ with zero mean. Its unique zero-mean periodic solution of $-\\Delta\\phi_\\varepsilon^\\mu=\\rho_\\varepsilon^\\mu$ is the absolutely and uniformly differentiable Fourier series $$ \\phi_\\varepsilon^\\mu(x)=L^{-d}\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^d\\setminus\\{0\\}} \\frac{\\left(\\prod_{a=1}^d\\alpha_\\varepsilon^{|k_a|}\\right)\\widehat\\mu(k)} {|\\kappa_k|^2}e^{i\\kappa_k\\cdot x}. $$\nFor every integer $r\\ge0$, all spatial derivative series of order at most $r$ converge absolutely and uniformly; their bounds may depend on $r,\\varepsilon,L,\\|\\mu\\|_{\\rm TV}$."
