    "statement": "Let $u:[0,T]\\times\\mathbb T_L^d\\to R$ have bounded spatial derivatives through order two, with $R$ a compact rectangle. Let $F\\in C^2$ on a neighborhood of $R$, and let $\\mathcal A_h=-D A_h^{\\rm per}$ be the periodic-grid diffusion generator from [[def-periodic-reaction-diffusion-grid]]. Define $F_h(P_hu)=P_h(F(u))$ pointwise. Then, uniformly over all periodic grids with $h_j=L_j/N_j$ and $N_j\\ge3$,\n$$\\sup_{\\substack{N_j\\ge3\\ (1\\le j\\le d),\\ 0\\le t\\le T}}\\left\\|\\mathcal A_hF_h(P_hu(t))-DF(P_hu(t))\\mathcal A_hP_hu(t)\\right\\|_\\infty\\le C_{\\rm com}<\\infty,$$\nwhere $C_{\\rm com}$ depends only on the dimension, $D$, the suprema of $D^2u$, $DF$, $D^2F$, and the compact state rectangle, not on the mesh widths. This is the finite-grid commutator used in the first-order split-error proof; it is not a claim for arbitrary meshes or unbounded operators."
