    "dependency_level": 1,
    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $F:\\widehat K\\to K$ be an admissible $C^1$ orientation-preserving cell diffeomorphism and let $u$ be $C^1$ on $K$. With $\\widehat u=u\\circ F$, one has $\\nabla_xu\\circ F=DF^{-T}\\nabla_{\\xi}\\widehat u$ and $\\int_K |\\nabla u|^2dx=\\int_{\\widehat K}J_F\\nabla\\widehat u^T(DF^{-1}DF^{-T})\\nabla\\widehat u\\,d\\xi$. For a regular $k$-dimensional parametrized face $f:U\\subset\\mathbb R^k\\to\\mathbb R^d$ with metric $G_f=Df^TDf$, the induced area factor is $\\sqrt{\\det G_f}$ and the tangential gradient of $u\\circ f$ is $DfG_f^{-1}\\nabla(u\\circ f)$; its squared norm is $\\nabla(u\\circ f)^TG_f^{-1}\\nabla(u\\circ f)$.",
