          ],
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "statement": "For a propagating angle $0\\le\\theta<\\pi/2$, $q=k\\cos\\theta$ and the one-way PML amplitude after accumulated stretch $S$ is $e^{-kS\\cos\\theta}$. It equals $e^{-kS}$ at normal incidence and tends to $1$ as $\\theta\\uparrow\\pi/2$. For a purely evanescent normal branch $q=i\\alpha$ with $\\alpha>0$, the factor $e^{iqX}=e^{-\\alpha x-i\\alpha S(x)}$ has modulus $e^{-\\alpha x}$, so this imaginary stretch adds no modulus decay.",
