          ],
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "statement": "Consider the one-dimensional interval $0\\le x\\le L$ with Dirichlet endpoints, source point $x_0=L/2$, and a PML beginning at $x_0$, so $X(x_0)=x_0$ and $X(L)=L+iS$ with $S>0$. For $kL=(2m+1)\\pi$, $m\\in\\mathbb N_0$, the Green function of $-d^2/dX^2-k^2$ at the source has magnitude\n$$|G(x_0,x_0)|=\\frac{\\coth(kS)}{k}\\sim\\frac1{k^2S}\\quad(S\\downarrow0).$$\nWhen $S=0$, $\\sin(kx)$ is a nonzero homogeneous Dirichlet mode, so the real-frequency problem is resonant. This is a single interval example, not a universal stability claim about PMLs.",
