          "statement": "Let $\\Omega=(0,L)$ and let $V_h$ be the conforming interval space in [[def-phase-field-discrete-realizations]], with center spacing $h$. Let $I_hv$ interpolate the absolutely-continuous representative of $v\\in H^1(0,L)$ at the centers and extend it constantly to the two boundary half-cells. Let $P_h$ be the exact $L^2$-orthogonal projection onto $V_h$. There is a constant $C$ independent of $h$ such that\n$$\\|I_hv\\|_{H^1}\\le C\\|v\\|_{H^1},\\qquad \\|v-I_hv\\|_{L^2}\\le Ch\\|v'\\|_{L^2},\\qquad \\|P_hv\\|_{H^1}\\le C\\|v\\|_{H^1}.$$\nIn addition, $\\|P_hv-v\\|_{L^2}\\le Ch\\|v'\\|_{L^2}$ for every $v\\in H^1(0,L)$, $P_hv\\to v$ in $H^1(0,L)$ for every $v\\in H^1(0,L)$, and $P_hg\\to g$ in $L^2(0,L)$ for every $g\\in L^2(0,L)$ as $h\\to0$.",
