    "statement": "Assume the finite-dimensional diffusion-transmission model of [[def-ale-linear-diffusion-transmission-model]]. Let $V:=\\{(v_1,v_2)\\in X_1\\oplus X_2:\\gamma_1v_1=\\gamma_2v_2\\}$ be the common-trace space, take $u^n\\in V$, and let $F_i^{n+1}\\in X_i$. In the block notation of the definition, set the local right-hand side to $g_i:=\\Delta t^{-1}M_i u_i^n+F_i^{n+1}$; assemble the local equations with common trace and the outward algebraic fluxes $q_i$ from that definition. There is a unique $u^{n+1}\\in V$ satisfying\n\n$$\\sum_{i=1}^2\\left(\\left\\langle M_i\\frac{u_i^{n+1}-u_i^n}{\\Delta t},v_i\\right\\rangle+\\langle A_i u_i^{n+1},v_i\\rangle\\right)=\\sum_{i=1}^2\\langle F_i^{n+1},v_i\\rangle\\qquad(v\\in V).$$\n\nIt obeys the exact identity\n\n$$\\frac12\\left(\\|u^{n+1}\\|_M^2-\\|u^n\\|_M^2+\\|u^{n+1}-u^n\\|_M^2\\right)+\\Delta t\\|u^{n+1}\\|_A^2=\\Delta t\\sum_{i=1}^2\\langle F_i^{n+1},u_i^{n+1}\\rangle,$$\n\nwhere $\\|v\\|_M^2:=\\sum_i\\langle M_iv_i,v_i\\rangle$ and $\\|v\\|_A^2:=\\sum_i\\langle A_iv_i,v_i\\rangle$. In the unforced case the monolithic backward-Euler energy is nonincreasing.",
