      "description": "{\"scope\": \"Define conforming variable-degree element spaces on an explicitly admissible matching mesh and polynomial-degree assignment, hierarchical basis, p/h/hp refinement, and a tensor-product Gauss–Lobatto spectral element on affine quadrilaterals/hexahedra. Prove p-explicit local approximation and inverse/trace inequalities, including degree factors in penalties/preconditioners. Derive energy error via NA29 with actual h,p,regularity dependence. Prove exponential p convergence for analytic solutions on a fixed regular mesh using a stated analytic derivative bound. For polygonal corner singularities prove exponential-in-a-power-of-DOF hp convergence only on the explicitly geometrically graded mesh and weighted-analytic regularity class, with the actual grading/degree law. Spectral-element GLL quadrature error is a Strang crime: mass/stiffness norms must be proved equivalent with p-uniform constants in the stated branch; do not equate collocation with exact Galerkin without checking quadrature.\", \"proof_route\": \"Construct reference interval polynomial projection using integrated orthogonal bases and derivative coefficient estimates; tensorize and transport with p-explicit constants. Prove face lifting/conforming assembly for varying degrees. Combine analytic derivative growth and factorial estimates to optimize truncation; for corners sum weighted layer approximation errors and count all DOFs to derive the claimed exponent. GLL norm equivalence and quadrature defects follow exactness plus explicit top-mode correction; variable coefficients require bounded smoothness and aliasing control. Root may select a 2D theorem first, but cannot infer its dimension exponent in 3D.\", \"examples\": \"analytic p refinement, corner singularity h versus hp, GLL mass top mode, p-dependent DG penalty failure.\"}",
      "items": [
  {
    "id": "def-hp-integrated-legendre-projector",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Endpoint-preserving integrated Legendre projector",
    "deps": [
