      "lem-legendre-weighted-derivative-orthogonality-and-norm"
    ],
    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 0,
    "statement": "For $p\\ge1$ and $g\\in L^2(-1,1)$, define the degree-$(p-1)$ Legendre orthogonal projection\n$$\n\\Pi_{p-1}g:=\\sum_{n=0}^{p-1}\\frac{2n+1}{2}\\left(\\int_{-1}^1g(t)P_n(t)\\,dt\\right)P_n.\n$$\nFor $c\\in\\mathbb R$, define the endpoint-anchored integrated projector\n$$\n\\mathcal I_p(c,g)(x):=c+\\int_{-1}^x\\Pi_{p-1}g(t)\\,dt,\\qquad -1\\le x\\le1.\n$$\nIf an absolutely continuous function $f$ is represented as $f(x)=f(-1)+\\int_{-1}^xf'(t)\\,dt$ with $f'\\in L^2$, write $I_pf:=\\mathcal I_p(f(-1),f')$. The finite sum and integral are defined for every such input; no choice axiom is used in this definition.",
    "source_path": "items/def-hp-integrated-legendre-projector.md",
    "local_order": 1,
    "provenance": {
