  {
    "id": "thm-hp-simplex-weighted-spectral-projection",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Weighted simplex polynomial projection has explicit p-rates",
    "deps": [
      "def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes"
    ],
    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 0,
    "statement": "Let $\\widehat K$ be the reference simplex of [[def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes]], let $\\alpha=(\\alpha_0,\\ldots,\\alpha_d)$ have nonnegative real entries, and let $\\omega_\\alpha=\\prod_{j=0}^d\\lambda_j^{\\alpha_j}$, where $\\lambda_j$ are its barycentric coordinates. Give polynomials the inner product $\\langle f,g\\rangle_\\alpha=\\int_{\\widehat K}\\omega_\\alpha fg$. Put $\\mathbb P_{-1}=\\{0\\}$ and let $E_n=\\mathbb P_n(\\widehat K)\\ominus\\mathbb P_{n-1}(\\widehat K)$ in this weighted inner product. For a finite sum $u=\\sum_{n\\ge0}u_n$, $u_n\\in E_n$, define\n$$\n\\|u\\|_{\\mathcal H_\\alpha^s}^2:=\\sum_{n\\ge0}(1+\\mu_n)^s\\|u_n\\|_{L^2(\\omega_\\alpha)}^2,\\qquad \\mu_n=n(n+d+|\\alpha|),\n$$\nand define $\\mathcal H_\\alpha^s$ as the completion of these finite sums. If $m\\ge\\ell\\ge0$, its orthogonal degree truncation $P_pu=\\sum_{n=0}^pu_n$ obeys\n$$\n\\|u-P_pu\\|_{\\mathcal H_\\alpha^\\ell}\\le(1+\\mu_{p+1})^{-(m-\\ell)/2}\\|u\\|_{\\mathcal H_\\alpha^m}.\n$$\nFor $q\\in\\mathbb P_p(\\widehat K)$, $\\|q\\|_{\\mathcal H_\\alpha^m}\\le(1+\\mu_p)^{(m-\\ell)/2}\\|q\\|_{\\mathcal H_\\alpha^\\ell}$. These are estimates in the explicitly coefficient-defined scale $\\mathcal H_\\alpha^s$; they do not identify that scale with ordinary unweighted $H^s(\\widehat K)$.",
    "source_path": "items/thm-hp-simplex-weighted-spectral-projection.md",
    "local_order": 5,
    "provenance": {
