    "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice for the $k\\ge1$ branch. Let $P_n$ be the real Legendre polynomial normalized by $P_n(1)=1$, and let $\\Pi_N$ be the $L^2(-1,1;\\mathbb R)$ orthogonal projection onto $\\mathbb P_N(-1,1)$. For every integer $k\\ge1$, every integer $N\\ge k-1$, and every real-valued $f\\in H^k(-1,1)$,\n\n$$\n\\|f-\\Pi_Nf\\|_{L^2(-1,1)}\\le\\left(\\frac{(N+1-k)!}{(N+1+k)!}\\right)^{1/2}\\|f^{(k)}\\|_{L^2(-1,1)}.\n$$\n\nFor $k=0$, every integer $N\\ge0$, and $f\\in L^2(-1,1)$, $\\|f-\\Pi_Nf\\|_2\\le\\|f\\|_2$. For $n,m\\ge k$ the repeated derivative orthogonality identity is\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1(1-x^2)^kP_n^{(k)}(x)P_m^{(k)}(x)\\,dx=\\frac{2}{2n+1}\\frac{(n+k)!}{(n-k)!}\\,\\delta_{nm}.\n$$",
