    "statement": "Fix an integer $p\\ge1$. Let $\\xi_0=-1$, $\\xi_p=1$, and let $\\xi_1<\\cdots<\\xi_{p-1}$ be the roots of $P_p'$ in $(-1,1)$; for $p=1$ this interior list is empty. By [[lem-legendre-gauss-lobatto-nodes-are-distinct]] these $p+1$ nodes are distinct. Define $\\ell_j(x)=\\prod_{0\\le i\\le p,\\ i\\ne j}(x-\\xi_i)/(\\xi_j-\\xi_i)$, set $w_j=\\int_{-1}^1\\ell_j(x)\\,dx$, and define the **Legendre–Gauss–Lobatto rule** by $Q_p(f)=\\sum_{j=0}^p w_jf(\\xi_j)$.\n\nOn $[-1,1]^d$ its tensor rule is $Q_p^{\\otimes d}(f)=\\sum_{j_1,\\ldots,j_d=0}^p(w_{j_1}\\cdots w_{j_d})f(\\xi_{j_1},\\ldots,\\xi_{j_d})$. For an affine box map $F_K(\\xi)=b_K+J_K\\xi$, define the transported rule by $Q_{K,p}(f)=|\\det J_K|Q_p^{\\otimes d}(f\\circ F_K)$. The nodal basis on $K$ is the pullback of $\\prod_{r=1}^d\\ell_{j_r}(\\xi_r)$. The local mass and stiffness forms are respectively $m_{K,p}(v,w)=Q_{K,p}(vw)$ and $a_{K,p}(v,w)=Q_{K,p}(\\nabla v\\cdot\\nabla w)$; any sampled coefficient is evaluated at the same quadrature nodes. Global forms are assembled by summing the cell forms.",
