    "id": "thm-isogeometric-elasticity-galerkin-quasioptimality",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Finite-Lamé isogeometric elasticity is conforming and quasi-optimal",
    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and the real displacement formulation of [[def-linear-elasticity-displacement-formulation-and-data]] on a nonempty bounded, connected Lipschitz domain $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$, $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$. Let $V=H^1_0(D;\\mathbb R^d)$ with the gradient norm, let the measurable shear modulus satisfy $0<\\mu_0\\le\\mu(x)\\le\\mu_1<\\infty$ almost everywhere, let $0\\le\\lambda<\\infty$, and let $f\\in V'$. For a finite conforming isogeometric subspace $V_h\\subset V$ built from the matching NURBS patches of [[def-isogeometric-galerkin-patch-space-and-refinement]], the elasticity variational problem has a unique solution $u$, the Galerkin problem has a unique solution $u_h$, and\n$$\\|u-u_h\\|_V\\le\\frac{2\\mu_1+d\\lambda}{\\mu_0}\\inf_{v_h\\in V_h}\\|u-v_h\\|_V.$$\nThe estimate is for each finite $\\lambda$ and has a factor growing with $\\lambda$; it is not a locking-free or $\\lambda$-uniform NURBS result.",
