    "id": "thm-nurbs-p1-tensor-spline-h1-error-rate",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Smooth compactly supported data have a degree-one NURBS energy rate",
    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $F:\\widehat\\Omega\\to D$ be one admissible NURBS patch, $\\widehat\\Omega=(0,1)^d$, $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$, with determinant upper bound $j_+$, derivative and inverse-derivative bound $L$, and continuous denominator $W$ that is $C^1$ on each knot cell, satisfies $W\\ge w_->0$, and has $\\|\\nabla W\\|_{L^\\infty}\\le G_W$. Let $g\\in C^1(\\overline{\\widehat\\Omega})$ have Lipschitz gradient with constant $M_g$ and support contained in a nonempty compact set $K\\Subset\\widehat\\Omega$, and set $\\widehat u=g/W$ and $u=\\widehat u\\circ F^{-1}$. Let the uniform tensor grid of side $h=1/N$ refine the geometry knot grid, let $S_h$ be its tensor-product degree-one $C^0$ numerator space, and let $V_h=\\{(s/W)\\circ F^{-1}:s\\in S_h\\}\\cap H^1_0(D)$ be the corresponding isogeometric trial space. Let $I_hg$ be the tensor Q1 nodal interpolant. If $h<\\operatorname{dist}(K,\\partial\\widehat\\Omega)/\\sqrt d$, then $v_h=(I_hg/W)\\circ F^{-1}$ belongs to $V_h$. If $u$ is the weak solution of an exact symmetric scalar elliptic problem with coefficient operator bound $\\beta$ and coercivity bound $\\alpha$ as in [[thm-isogeometric-poisson-galerkin-quasioptimality]], and $u_h$ its exact-form isogeometric Galerkin solution in $V_h$, then\n$$\\|u-u_h\\|_{H^1_0(D),\\nabla}\\le\\frac\\beta\\alpha\\,C_F C_W C_d\\,hM_g,$$\nwhere $C_F=\\sqrt{j_+}\\sqrt{1+L^2}$, $C_W=2/w_-+G_W/w_-^2$, and $C_d=d+\\sqrt d+2^{d-1}d\\sqrt d$. These constants retain their map, weight, coefficient, and dimension dependence. This proves only the degree-one compact-support branch; it is not a general high-degree, knot-family, or locking-free rate.",
