    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 0,
    "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$, $T>0$, $\\ell_j>0$, and let $J\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an open interval containing $[0,T]$. Suppose $b:J\\times\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R^d$ is $C^1$ and periodic in $x_j$ with period $\\ell_j$ for every $j$. Choose a compact interval $K\\subset J$ with $[0,T]\\subset\\operatorname{int}K$, and put $M_K:=\\sup_{K\\times[0,\\ell_1]\\times\\cdots\\times[0,\\ell_d]}\\|b\\|_2$. For every $s\\in[0,T]$ and $x\\in\\mathbb R^d$, there is a unique solution $X(\\cdot;s,x)$ of\n$$X'(t)=b(t,X(t)),\\qquad X(s;s,x)=x,$$\non the whole interval $[0,T]$. The lifted flow is periodic-equivariant:\n$$X(t;s,x+\\boldsymbol k\\boldsymbol\\ell)=X(t;s,x)+\\boldsymbol k\\boldsymbol\\ell\\qquad(\\boldsymbol k\\in\\mathbb Z^d),$$\nwhere $\\boldsymbol k\\boldsymbol\\ell=(k_1\\ell_1,\\ldots,k_d\\ell_d)$. If $M_T:=\\sup_{[0,T]\\times[0,\\ell_1]\\times\\cdots\\times[0,\\ell_d]}\\|b\\|_2$, then\n$$\\|X(t;s,x)-x\\|_2\\le M_T|t-s|\\qquad(t\\in[0,T]).$$\nThus each characteristic stays in a compact tube $[0,T]\\times\\overline B(x,M_TT+1)$.",
