    "dependency_level": 2,
    "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $\\Omega=\\prod_{j=1}^d(0,\\ell_j)$ be the bounded open fundamental box used for Lebesgue measure, and let $Q=\\prod_{j=1}^d[0,\\ell_j)$ be its half-open grid-indexing copy. Let $\\Phi$ be the periodic $C^1$ characteristic diffeomorphism of [[lem-periodic-characteristic-map-is-orientation-preserving]], and let $A_i\\subseteq Q$ be a Lebesgue-measurable arrival cell with $|A_i|:=\\lambda_d(A_i\\cap\\Omega)>0$. Then $D_i:=\\Phi^{-1}(A_i)$, interpreted on the torus and represented in $\\Omega$, is Lebesgue measurable and satisfies\n$$0<|D_i|<\\infty.$$\nThis includes every finite tensor-grid cell with nonempty interior. The departure cells form a partition up to null sets whenever a finite family of arrival cells does; an exact torus partition pulls back to an exact torus partition.",
